son:660:    \\\"description\\\": \\\"全网格输出中，箭头精灵替代开放框，路径为纯直线从触点沿箭头方向贯穿到对边。保持原始尺寸同时可见箭头和内部射线，视觉关联增强。\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py:103:    Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py:169:\\\"\\\"\\\"Generator for task 88e364bc (slide yellow in walled regions by legend arrows).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_16b78196_merged_report.json:1405:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"终止标记精灵+方向箭头\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_16b78196_merged_report.json:1410:    \\\"description\\\": \\\"链终止由特殊颜色的终止精灵标记（灰色精灵插入后链结束），有效缺口旁有箭头状标记指示链的生长方向。solver需：(1)解读缺口旁的方向标记确定链生长朝向，(2)识别终止精灵的特殊语义，(3)在方向标记指引下按序拼装直到遇到终止标记。两种符号系统协同工作：箭头指引开始和方向，特殊色指示结束。\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:7:    Trace diagonal rays from triangular arrows, reflecting off colored wall pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:10:    - bg grid with monochrome 3-pixel L-shaped \\\"arrows\\\" (2x2 bbox missing one corner) and scattered colored wall pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:13:    - Each arrow fires a ray diagonally away from its missing corner, painting bg cells in its color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:16:    - Ray stops when it exits the grid or reaches another arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:24:    def is_arrow_pts(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:31:    def arrow_dir_and_start(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:54:    # Detect arrows per-color (cannot rely on global non-bg connectivity).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:55:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:56:    arrows: list[tuple[int, list[tuple[int, int]]]] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:60:            if is_arrow_pts(pts):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:61:                arrows.append((int(col), pts))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:62:                arrow_cells |= set(pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:65:        (int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(g != int(bg)) if (int(r), int(c)) not in arrow_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:70:    for start_col, pts in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:71:        info = arrow_dir_and_start(pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:99:            if (nr, nc) in arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:143:    Output-first: for each arrow, plan the full zigzag ray path (with 0-4 side-touch\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:144:    bounces), place walls at bounce points, then derive the input (arrows + walls).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:147:    n_arrows = _rng.randint(1, 7)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:150:    arrow_colors = palette[:n_arrows]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:156:    for ai in range(n_arrows):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:157:        color = arrow_colors[ai]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:163:            # Start position with room for the 2x2 arrow bbox\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:172:            arrow_pts = [(r, c) for r in (mr, sr) for c in (mc, sc) if (r, c) != (mr, mc)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:173:            if any(not (0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W) or (r, c) in occupied for r, c in arrow_pts):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:181:            arrow_set = set(arrow_pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:203:                    if (nr, nc) in occupied or (nr, nc) in ray_set or (nr, nc) in arrow_set:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:240:                    if any((r, c) in occupied or (r, c) in ray_set or (r, c) in arrow_set\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:266:            new_cells = set(arrow_pts) | ray_set\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:269:            expected_count = len(arrow_pts) + len(ray_cells) + sum(len(w) for w, _ in walls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:274:            for r, c in arrow_pts:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py:22:    Key insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py:216:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py:217:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/247ef758.py:39:    - bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/5545f144.py:196:    - Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:11:# In the input, you will see several objects of the same color that are in an arrowhead shape and facing different directions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:12:# The goal is to find the directions of the arrowheads and draw lines that would represent the path they had been moving in to go in that direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:16:    Extend each small arrowhead with a line in the direction it points.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:19:    - The input is a black grid with several same-colored arrowhead objects.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:20:    - Each arrowhead is a small shape whose missing corner indicates its direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:21:    - Lines should use the arrowhead color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:24:    - Crop each arrowhead and compare the mean positions of colored and black cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:26:    - Draw a line from the matching outer corner of the arrowhead's bounding box to the grid edge.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:29:    - The arrowhead asymmetry identifies both the direction of travel and the corner where the path begins.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:37:    # for each object, find the direction the arrowhead is pointing in by finding the relative mean position of colored and black pixels in the bounding box of the object\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:60:        # find the direction the arrowhead is pointing in, it is from the mean position of the colored pixels to the mean position of the black pixels\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:63:        # draw a line in the direction the arrowhead is pointing in from the corresponding corner of the bounding box\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:70:            # check if the corner is in the direction that the arrowhead is pointing\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:81:    # choose the color of the arrowheads\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:84:    # make the arrowheads by making a 2x2 square then removing one of the corners randomly and placing it randomly on the grid\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:86:        # make at arrowhead\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:87:        arrowhead = np.full((2, 2), color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:89:        arrowhead[corner // 2, corner % 2] = Color.BLACK\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:92:        _loc = first_free_location(grid, arrowhead, transparent=Color.BLACK, border=0, padding=1, padding_connectivity=8)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:96:        paste(grid, arrowhead, r, c, transparent=Color.BLACK, clip=True)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/28/code.py:29:#    2x4 horizontal arrow, a near-square inner frame, and a 4x2 vertical arrow, the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头指示方向+L形框架\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:12:  3-pixel L-triomino arrow placed just outside one side of that cup.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:14:  visual L frame, either endpoint could be the ejecting endpoint; the nearby arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:22:     endpoint on the side indicated by the external arrow component. The content\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:24:     the arrow-selected endpoint is first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:26:     a straight line from that endpoint in the arrow-indicated direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:29:  - direction cue changed: inferred from shape -> read from nearby arrow component\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:33:- The arrow vocabulary is tiny: one fixed 3-cell 2x2-L component, placed on one of\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:37:  three leg relations for the arrow-selected endpoint: shorter, equal, and longer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:38:  than the other endpoint's first leg. Equal-leg cups especially force the arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:44:  each cup color appears as two components, the body and its arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:48:  construction; the arrow can choose the longer endpoint or an equal-leg case.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:50:  1. find L-body components and L-arrow components separately,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:51:  2. pair an L body with the unique same-color arrow lying completely beyond one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:53:  3. orient the body path so that its tail direction matches that arrow side,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:58:- The generator builds each cup output-first: body + arrow + ejection line, then\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:60:- Cup+arrow combo bboxes keep a 1-cell gap from each other via dilated placement.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:68:  output line leaves from the endpoint nearest the small same-color arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:69:- Because equal-leg and arrow-to-longer-endpoint cases are common, shape-only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:70:  explanations fail; the arrow is the only stable cue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:74:- The arrow is kept close to its cup but separated by at least one empty row/col,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:76:- The arrow is offset away from the exact ejection ray, so it remains visible in\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:81:- No color remapping is introduced. The arrow simply reuses the cup border color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:83:  border colors, so humans and the solver can associate each arrow to its cup by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:88:- Assumption: each cup border color has exactly one L-body component and one arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:90:- Assumption: the arrow lies completely beyond exactly one side of the cup body's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:92:  arrow templates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:94:  has a tail direction matching the arrow side. Guaranteed by how each cup is built.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:235:def _is_arrow_component(cell_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:242:def _arrow_side(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:243:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:246:    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = _component_bbox(arrow_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:266:      same-color 3-cell arrow component on one side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:267:    - The arrow side selects which endpoint of the L is the spike.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:269:      endpoint in the arrow-indicated direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:282:        arrow_components = [comp for comp in comps if _is_arrow_component(comp)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:293:            matched_arrows = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:294:            for arrow_set in arrow_components:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:295:                side = _arrow_side(arrow_set, body_bbox)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:297:                    matched_arrows.append((side, arrow_set))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:298:            if len(matched_arrows) != 1:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:301:            tail_dir = matched_arrows[0][0]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:422:def _arrow_templates_for_body(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:460:def _attach_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:469:    arrow_template = _arrow_templates_for_body(tail_dir, spike, body_patch.shape)[int(rng.integers(0, 2))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:470:    arrow_coords = [(spike[0] + dr, spike[1] + dc) for dr, dc in arrow_template]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:472:    all_coords = body_coords + arrow_coords\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:481:    for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/8/code.py:616:    patch, spike, mouth, body_bbox_local = _attach_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头方向+矩形框架+边缘控制像素\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:29:       2. tail direction comes from a same-color 3-pixel L arrow attached beside the closed side,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:32:   - Small trace: suppose a cup body is a tail-up rectangle, with a small same-color arrow above it and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:34:     arrow conceptually, recognize the remaining component as an upward rectangular cup, infer UP from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:35:     the arrow placement, count the four orange edge controls, erase those controls, and draw four orange\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:43:   - The arrow is fixed to a 3-cell L triomino, reused across all examples, so direction remains\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:52:   - \\\"Full component equals cup body\\\" is false because the arrow is attached to the border component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:57:       1. enumerate 3-cell L arrow candidates on each border component,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:59:       3. infer direction from the arrow side relative to the recovered cup bbox,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:65:     controls never overlap the cup itself. The arrow may approach or touch a non-control border side;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:67:   - Cup+arrow components keep at least a 1-cell gap from each other via 8-neighborhood dilation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:68:   - Ejection rays are reserved globally so no cup body, arrow, or later ray occupies another ray.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:73:   - Across examples a human sees: empty rectangular cups, same-color arrows attached near the closed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:76:   - Direction is not encoded by numeric color id; it is visible from local arrow placement.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:83:   - The arrow sits off the ejection ray, so it remains visible in both input and output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:87:     directly visible: the cup geometry is rectangular, direction is a local arrow marker, and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:92:   - Assumption: each relevant border component contains exactly one removable 3-cell L arrow whose\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:93:     removal yields an exact rectangular cup. Guaranteed by `_attach_arrow`.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:94:   - Assumption: the arrow lies completely outside exactly one side of the recovered cup bbox. Guaranteed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:95:     by the fixed arrow templates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:190:def _enumerate_arrow_candidates(border_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[set[tuple[int, int]]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:243:def _arrow_side(arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]], cup_bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> str | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:244:    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(np.array(sorted(arrow_cells), dtype=int))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:272:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Recover the cup body by stripping one arrow candidate from the merged component.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:274:    for arrow_cells in _enumerate_arrow_candidates(border_set):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:275:        cup_set = border_set - arrow_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:280:        tail_dir = _arrow_side(arrow_cells, cup_bbox)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:299:                \\\"arrow_cells\\\": set(arrow_cells),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:335:    - A same-color 3-pixel arrow attached beside the closed side tells the ejection direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:472:def _attach_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:479:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Attach the same-color L arrow beside the closed side of the rectangular cup.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:481:    arrow_template = ARROW_OFFSETS[direction][int(rng.integers(0, 2))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:482:    arrow_coords = [(spike[0] + dr, spike[1] + dc) for dr, dc in arrow_template]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:484:    all_coords = border_coords + arrow_coords\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:493:    for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:536:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place the combined cup+arrow patch away from the border with a clear reserved ray.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/37/code.py:664:    patch, spike, cup_bbox_local = _attach_arrow(rng, patch_body, spike_body, direction, border_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/689c358e.py:73:    Mark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/689c358e.py:77:    - Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头指示方向+矩形框架\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:6:Fusion variant of 3dc255db: rectangular 3-sided cups plus detached arrow markers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:18:     detached same-color 3-pixel L arrow sits just outside one of the frame's closed sides. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:19:     mouth is determined from the open side; the spike is the center pixel of the arrow-indicated\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:21:   - Example: a 5x5 frame open downward can now eject upward, leftward, or rightward. If the arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:28:   - The arrow vocabulary is small: a detached 3-cell L triomino, with two offset variants per\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:36:     border color is split across a frame component and a detached arrow component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:38:     opening only determines the mouth; the arrow chooses among the three closed sides.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:40:     side, not from the side opposite the arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:43:       2. the associated arrow is a detached 3-cell 2x2-L component of the same color;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:44:       3. the arrow lies exactly one blank cell beyond one frame side and overlaps that side's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:50:   - Generator builds the output state first: cup frame + detached arrow + ejected line.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:51:   - Combined occupied cells of cup and arrow keep an 8-neighborhood gap from other cups/arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:54:   - The arrow is offset away from the ray, so the output line never overwrites the marker.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:58:   - The detached arrow is plainly visible on one closed side, so humans can see that ejection is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:65:   - Cups, arrows, and rays are kept disjoint across objects.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:69:   - No new color mapping is introduced. The arrow reuses the frame color, so the association is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:76:   - Assumption: exactly one nearby L-arrow of the same color lies one cell beyond a closed side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:77:     Guaranteed by fixed arrow templates and unique border colors per cup.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:211:def _is_l_arrow_component(cells: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:212:    \\\"\\\"\\\"3-cell detached arrow sprite: an L triomino inside a 2x2 bbox.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:232:def _arrow_side(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:233:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:236:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Infer which cup side the detached arrow marks.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:237:    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = (int(v) for v in bbox_coords(np.array(sorted(arrow_cells), dtype=int)))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:255:    - A detached same-color 3-pixel L arrow picks one closed side as the tail.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:273:        arrow_candidates: list[set[tuple[int, int]]] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:276:            if _is_l_arrow_component(comp_set):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:277:                arrow_candidates.append(comp_set)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:315:            for arrow_cells in arrow_candidates:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:316:                tail_dir = _arrow_side(arrow_cells, bbox)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:363:def _attach_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:370:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a combined patch containing the frame and a detached arrow.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:378:    arrow_template = ARROW_OFFSETS[tail_dir][int(rng.integers(0, 2))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:379:    arrow_coords = [(spike[0] + dr, spike[1] + dc) for dr, dc in arrow_template]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:380:    all_coords = body_coords + arrow_coords\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:390:    for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:430:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place one cup+arrow combo while preserving spacing and a clear ray to the edge.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:538:    combo_patch, spike, mouth, body_bbox_local = _attach_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/0a938d79.py:81:    # make a grid that is narrow and tall. This is for horizontal lines, and we will flip a coin at the end to transpose everything to make things vertical\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/30/code.py:32:#      canvases, so the count range is intentionally narrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/1/code.py:31:#      the color-choice hypothesis narrow and repeated across the full training set.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/33/code.py:36:#    The cascade is intentionally narrow: one ordered chain, one visible comparison key per step, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:3:# Name: 带对角标记的精灵+方向箭头标记\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:15:#   a 2-pixel arrow stub made from the transferable payload color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:19:#   source.arrow -> dominant-axis direction to the target destination,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:32:#   in the encoded arrow direction. So arrow direction alone is insufficient.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:34:#   corners compatible with the chosen arrow direction. This keeps the symbolic alphabet small.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:42:#   that border class and then resolve the target by arrow direction plus marker quadrant.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:43:# - The D15-style directional cue is compressed to a 2-pixel center+neighbor arrow stub. That\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:46:#   3-pixel arrow while remaining a single readable object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:51:# - Sources are always fully visible 3x3 boxes so both the arrow and the diagonal marker are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:53:# - Source placement is filtered so the two destinations are both in the source's arrow direction\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:58:# - The input visibly contains two deleted source boxes, each with an arrow and an extra corner\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:65:# - The arrow is a compact 2-pixel center+edge pointer, while the marker remains a single corner\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:75:# - For each real source, both destinations share the arrow direction but occupy the two marker\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:152:    assert patch[mr, mc] == border_color, \\\"marker corner must not overlap the arrow\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:409:def _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g: np.ndarray, bg: int, grey: int) -> list[dict]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:412:    The payload forms one of four 2-pixel arrow stubs and includes the center cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:413:    The marker is a singleton corner not occupied by the arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:523:    - Each real source box has three simultaneous parts: a shared border color, a 2-pixel payload-colored arrow stub, and one extra diagonal marker pixel in a corner.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:529:    - Among those same-border candidates, keep the unique source whose arrow points toward the destination and whose diagonal marker corner matches the destination's quadrant relative to that source.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:533:    - Matching is now layered: the destination center color selects a source border class, the arrow gives a coarse global direction, and the diagonal marker resolves which destination inside that direction cone is the true target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:540:    sources = _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g, bg, grey)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:542:    assert sources, \\\"expected marked arrow sources\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:770:    sources = _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g, bg, GREY)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:23:      - 每个起点边上紧贴一个箭头色像素, 箭头偏移方向就是初始方向; solver 不再从边界位置硬推方向。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:25:      - 以左侧组件为例, 粒子在 `(r,0)` 且 `(r,1)` 是箭头, 因此先向右。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:32:    - 同一张图里固定出现四条边的起点, 且四个组件共享同一个可见模板, 便于人类从 2-4 个样例里归纳“边缘粒子 + 箭头 + 长路径追踪”。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:33:    - 颜色自由度被压到少量档位: 4 个走廊色、1 个箭头色、1 个背景色、1 个粒子色。颜色不编码隐藏语义, 只承担“同色墙/异色 breaker”的可见结构作用。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:35:    - 原 `_trace` 把初始方向写死为 `right`; 融合后必须改成读取箭头。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:36:    - 原 `_has_corridor` 只把 `{BG, PARTICLE}` 视作可走; 融合后箭头像素必须是可通行的, 否则粒子一出发就撞上标记。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:40:    - D5 与 D15 叠加后的潜在冲突是“方向会不会又退化成由边缘唯一决定”; 这里用显式箭头作为 solver 的唯一方向来源, 代码层面不再读取边的位置来推方向。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:47:    - 人类能直接看到四条边上各有一个品红粒子, 且粒子旁都有同色箭头标记。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:49:    - 规则完全由相邻关系、夹道同色、箭头偏移三种可见线索决定, 不依赖颜色编号或隐式排序。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:51:    - 箭头只出现在起点旁, 不会与内部墙体混在一起。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:58:    - solver 假设有效起点是边界粒子且拥有唯一相邻箭头。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:59:      generator 保证每个真实起点都满足这一点, 且没有额外伪箭头贴在粒子周围。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:134:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return border particles that have exactly one adjacent arrow marker.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:193:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Move magenta edge particles by following explicit arrows through spiral corridors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:196:    - bg=7, particle=6, arrow=2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:198:    - Each valid particle has exactly one adjacent arrow pixel; that offset gives the initial direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:202:    - Start each edge particle in the arrow-indicated direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:203:    - Move straight through passable cells (`bg`, `particle`, `arrow`).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:211:      change the tracing rule; only the arrow-selected initial direction changes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/19/code.py:26:#    - `main()` launch-row detection assumed many bar colors might exist, but its real requirement is narrower:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:82:#   1. narrow lanes move, wide lanes do not;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:89:# - The scene remains a small set of repeated elements: bar rows, narrow/wide\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:263:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Move magenta particles through dashed narrow corridors with bounded gap crossing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:19:      - 每个粒子旁边多一个固定颜色的箭头像素; 粒子到箭头像素的相对偏移就是初始方向。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:20:      - 左边起点表现为 `(row,0)=particle, (row,1)=arrow`; 右边是 `(row,W-1)=particle, (row,W-2)=arrow`;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:21:        顶/底边分别把箭头放在粒子正下/正上。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:24:      - 融合后: 若粒子在顶边 `(0,c_v-1)`, 箭头在 `(1,c_v-1)`, solver 先从箭头偏移读出 `down`,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:29:    - 箭头只用一个专用颜色, 避免引入额外颜色映射。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:31:    - 箭头保持朝向网格内部的真实通路端点; 若让箭头沿边切向移动, 需要额外边界引导结构, 会把任务改得过重。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:33:    - 原 `_trace` 写死 `right`; 组合后必须改成参数, 且箭头像素必须视为可通行。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:34:    - 原 `main` 只扫描 `col 0`; 组合后必须扫描四条边, 并从唯一相邻箭头恢复方向。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:35:    - 原 `_has_corridor` 只把 `BG/PARTICLE` 当作可通行; 组合后若不把 `ARROW` 也算 passable, 起步时就会被箭头挡住。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:36:    - 原 generator 会无条件铺满 `col 0` 粒子; 组合后绝不能这样做, 否则会覆盖右/顶/底起点和箭头。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:38:    - 新 solver 额外假设: 每个有效边界粒子恰有一个 4 邻箭头。generator 通过专门放置并校验 `_edge_starts` 来保证。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:43:    - 箭头永远落在粒子的内侧相邻可通行格, 不与彩墙重叠, 不越界。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:45:    - 样例中会同时看到左/右/上/下四种边界起点, 且每个起点都带同色箭头标记, 人类可直接归纳“箭头给初始方向”。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:46:    - 输出只移动粒子, 不删除箭头, 因此输入中的起始证据在输出里仍可对照。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:49:    - 箭头只出现在边界起点旁, 不进入内部转弯区, 不与假走廊装饰混叠。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:50:    - 走廊仍是单层结构: 彩条=墙, BG/箭头=可走区域, 品红=被移动对象。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:52:    - 颜色机制只保留原题的“同色夹墙可转弯”; 箭头颜色固定且不参与颜色映射。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:54:    - solver 假设有效起点都在边界且恰有一个箭头邻居; generator 在放置后调用 `_edge_starts` 验证。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:56:    - solver 假设箭头方向确实通向可通行路径; generator 只从 `_candidate_starts_for_plan` 产出的合法端点放置起点。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:118:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return border particles whose unique adjacent arrow pixel defines the start direction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:183:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Move arrow-marked edge particles through same-color corridors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:186:    - bg=7, particle=6, arrow marker=2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:188:    - Particles may appear on any of the four grid edges, each with exactly one adjacent arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:191:    - The arrow offset relative to a border particle gives its initial direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:192:    - The particle moves straight through passable cells (bg, particle, arrow).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:199:      You must first read each edge particle's adjacent arrow to recover the initial\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:630:def _place_particles_and_arrows(g: np.ndarray, starts: list[tuple[int, int, str]]) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:631:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place particles on the border and their unique adjacent arrow markers.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:633:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:641:        if (ar, ac) in arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:645:        arrow_cells.add((ar, ac))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:709:    if not _place_particles_and_arrows(g, starts):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:124:    \\\"\\\"\\\"True iff (r,c) is inside a real narrow corridor under the fused rule.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:163:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Move magenta particles through broken narrow corridors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:174:    - The particle stops at the grid edge or when no valid narrow turn exists.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:178:      the narrow 1-row gap whose two dashed rails are still visible within radius 1, even if\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/6/code.py:74:#      to narrow strips on the middle box / inner box edges.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/11/code.py:43:#    - Free parameters are kept narrow: only three spiral columns vary per path,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/7/code.py:28:# - The palette remains in the original narrow regime: four non-bg/non-particle\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/43/code.py:68:#       combo outputs differ from a narrow unbounded baseline on the same inputs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/49/code.py:26:#     The family is intentionally narrow: one basin template, one erasable source component, one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:20:#      * The same seed line also touches a U-shaped pocket whose 5-region reaches the top edge through a narrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/36/code.py:21:#    \\\"any enclosed hole\\\" logic is therefore narrowed to \\\"interiors of detected rectangle\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/18/code.py:35:#    - The basin family is deliberately narrow: two adjacent cups with an optional overflow divider.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/25/code.py:35:#    - this fusion narrows the true transform family to morphology, introduces a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/43/code.py:16:#      The generated landform is a high right-side shelf beside a narrow vertical chute; a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/25/code.py:37:#    The family is deliberately narrow:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:431:def _add_right_source(g: np.ndarray, top_row: int, narrow_rows: int, color: int) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:474:        narrow_rows = 0\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:482:        _add_right_source(g, right_top, narrow_rows, right_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/42/code.py:21:#      generator narrows legal exits to one corner gap per frame, so every beam is diagonal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/27/code.py:25:# - The geometry is deliberately narrow: always two adjacent basins, always a shorter\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/20/code.py:38:#   narrow, which guarantees a visible disagreement between pixel-majority and side-vote\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/2/code.py:26:#      keeps the visual degree of freedom narrow and repeatable across 2-4 ARC examples.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/8/code.py:17:#    - The fused change fixes the lower area to a long chain of 4 or 5 narrow basins. The top\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/8/code.py:288:    - Bottom-anchored solids form a chain of 4 or 5 narrow basins separated by single divider walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:44:#      narrows the target to the two blue-striped holes. One hole shows a red\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:19:#       1) use the arrow between the two training frames to read source -> destination,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:31:#         - read the arrow to fix direction,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:45:#     - The arrow only appears between horizontally or vertically adjacent training frames, which keeps the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:49:#       invalid once direction is explicitly marked, so the solver now decodes the arrow first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:58:#       for a thin arrow to fit between any allowed training pair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:59:#     - Sprite pixels live strictly inside frame interiors. The arrow is drawn only in the corridor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:62:#     - A human can see the arrow before reasoning about the transform.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:84:#     - `decode_training_direction()` assumes one isolated arrow component sits in the gap between the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:341:        arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:342:        if arrow == \\\"right\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:344:        if arrow == \\\"left\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:373:    arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:374:    if arrow == \\\"down\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:376:    if arrow == \\\"up\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:383:    Solve a framed sprite analogy where a directed arrow and three color roles specify a contour rule.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:389:    - A thin single-color arrow lies between the two training frames and points from the example source\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:393:    - Match the training pair by identical non-zero palettes, then decode the arrow to determine the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:401:    - The arrow removes direction ambiguity, while the color counts reveal the stable role.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:662:def draw_direction_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:813:    draw_direction_arrow(grid, frame_boxes[train_direction[0]], frame_boxes[train_direction[1]], marker_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/24/code.py:37:#    - or, for the narrower layout, the same receiver with one inner step.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/29/code.py:57:    arrow\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/29/code.py:96:    color matches and visible arrow orientation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/29/code.py:249:      color match between a side-mounted legend and its chamber wall; the arrow orientation inside that\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:14:#      then both training frames and both test/blank frames have right-edge gaps, and a thin arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:19:#      corridor arrow -> transform the test sprite -> write it into the blank frame -> return the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:27:#    - The arrow and the frame gaps encode the same direction redundantly. That redundancy is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:34:#      both the gap side and the arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:40:#    - Frames are placed on a 2x2 structured layout with minimum corridor width, so arrows fit\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:43:#      erased -> interior sprite pasted -> corridor arrows drawn. This keeps each layer separable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:45:#    - A human sees four obviously broken frames, two arrows, and one empty destination frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:54:#      original rule families, while direction is conveyed structurally by gap orientation and arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:481:def decode_arrow_direction(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:576:    arrow_dir = decode_arrow_direction(grid, frames, pair)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:577:    if gap_dir is None or arrow_dir is None or gap_dir != arrow_dir:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:602:    - The training pair and the test/blank pair each have a thin arrow in the corridor between them,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:603:      and the arrow direction matches the shared gap side of that pair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:607:      the source->destination order from the combined gap-side cue and corridor arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:1026:def draw_direction_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:1169:    draw_direction_arrow(grid, frame_boxes[train_dir[0]], frame_boxes[train_dir[1]], marker_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/20/code.py:1170:    draw_direction_arrow(grid, frame_boxes[test_blank_dir[0]], frame_boxes[test_blank_dir[1]], marker_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/33/code.py:33:#    The geometry is intentionally narrow and repetitive rather than highly free-form:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:53:#    - 图例的两个红点一横一竖，非常直观地提示“这不是一个单向箭头，而是两阶段正交指令”。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:395:    - The legend no longer means one atomic arrow. It encodes two cardinal sub-moves, and the fixed processing order is part of the rule: horizontal first, vertical second.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/11/code.py:30:#    - The geometry family is intentionally narrow: one top source shelf and three shaft mouths.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/41/code.py:35:#    - The rule is intentionally narrowed to straight rays and single-gap generated samples. This keeps the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:23:#       - then each mover reads the arrow tied to its own color inside that legend;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:25:#         pink stays at its input cell even if its arrow points into open space.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:33:#       the same visible mover color now selects both which arrow to read and how much of that\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:67:#     - Pink is only accepted when its own arrow has at least one open step ahead, so \\\"pink does\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:257:    Slide multi-colored mover pixels inside sealed wall regions using color-specific arrows and color-specific travel lengths.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:272:    - Wall color chooses which legend applies, while mover color chooses both which arrow to read inside that legend and how much of the available path to traverse.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/25/code.py:353:    raise RuntimeError(\\\"_sample_legend_dirs: unable to place non-overlapping color-specific arrows\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/17/code.py:32:#     - tabs are narrower than the strip, which makes concave/convex shoulders visible without exploding the case count\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/5/code.py:13:# - The generator uses narrow funnel chambers so both changes are externally visible:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/14/code.py:35:#    - \\\"holes can be found anywhere inside the bbox\\\" is narrowed to rectangular bg\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:18:#   - D11/0 removes direction guessing. A thin arrow is drawn in the corridor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:30:#       3. decode the arrow so direction is fixed before rule inference\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:44:#     after adding a dedicated anchor color, an arrow color, a frame color, and a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:51:#   - find_square_frames() still works because the arrow never touches a frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:57:#     explicit and should be decoded from the arrow instead of guessed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:62:#     * the training pair is axis-adjacent with a unique arrow component in its gap\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:68:#     and column gap, so the arrow fits cleanly between adjacent training frames.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:69:#   - The arrow is drawn only in the corridor between the chosen pair and never\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:78:#   - The arrow is a separate unique-color component outside all frames, so it does\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:90:#     repeats the same joint pattern: arrow fixes direction, anchor stays fixed,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:333:        arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:334:        if arrow == \\\"right\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:336:        if arrow == \\\"left\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:365:    arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:366:    if arrow == \\\"down\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:368:    if arrow == \\\"up\\\":\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:375:    Learn an anchor-aware contour rule from a framed training pair with an explicit arrow, then solve the test sprite.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:380:    - Every non-blank sprite contains exactly one shared-color anchor pixel, and a thin arrow outside the frames points from the training source frame to the training destination frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:384:    - Use the arrow to decide the training direction, then verify that the destination equals the 4-connected outer boundary of the source body, where the body means all non-zero pixels except the anchor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:388:    - The anchor is not ordinary foreground. It stays visible but should be mentally removed before tracing the body's outline, and the arrow removes any need to guess which training frame is the source.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:604:def draw_direction_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/9/code.py:695:    draw_direction_arrow(grid, frame_boxes[train_direction[0]], frame_boxes[train_direction[1]], marker_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:78:    - using only cardinal arrows avoids mixing the D6 geometric effect with diagonal corner-cutting\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:88:    - the fused change is inferable from shape geometry plus arrow direction, not from numeric color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:63:#      one narrower opening so the contrast is present within each grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:758:    narrow_candidates = [i for i, available in enumerate(available_per_block) if i != wide_idx and (1 in available or 2 in available)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:759:    if not narrow_candidates:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:761:    narrow_idx = narrow_candidates[int(rng.integers(len(narrow_candidates)))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:767:        elif i == narrow_idx:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:768:            narrow_sizes = [size for size in (1, 2) if size in available]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:769:            size = narrow_sizes[int(rng.integers(len(narrow_sizes)))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/7/code.py:42:#      narrow basin columns bounded by walls or grid edges; final water still occupies complete\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/32/code.py:32:        - at a narrow elbow the bridge square exists but the parallel lane disappears, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/32/code.py:35:        - two yellows under the same arrow can end at different depths: one reaches the remote\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/32/code.py:317:    - The wall color still chooses the arrow, but the final resting place now depends on both the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/12/code.py:127:    Key insight: The puzzle is solved by a genuine two-step cue hierarchy: size only says which pieces can fit, marker count narrows the candidate slot set, and the marker layout inside equally counted rectangles determines the final correspondence.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:378:    Launch wall-jammed yellow pixels using the legend arrows, with the touching wall causing the first rebound and later wall hits continuing the reflected path.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:390:    - The yellow pixels are not supposed to reverse-slide directly; they must be fired along the legend arrow from a wall-touching start, so the initial wall contact determines the rebound and the rest of the reflected route.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/27/code.py:78:#     visible legend arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/32/code.py:228:    - Bottom-anchored divider columns create 4 or 5 narrow basins along the lower edge; a short upper platform supports the source,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:46:  - Room interiors are narrow in the stacking axis and longer in the motion axis, which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/33/code.py:167:      the arrow-like offset inside the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:78:   - Restricting the generator to a narrow family of odd hollow frames makes the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:43:    - B-only rooms no longer follow B's shown arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:65:      with three colors and a centroid-based arrow cue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:87:  - The A-only room anchors the normal meaning of a legend arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:88:  - The B-only room shows that B's displayed arrow is not the real motion cue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:109:      uses B's displayed arrow directly instead of sign(disp_A - disp_B).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:342:    two-legend rule instead of a one-color one-arrow lookup.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:353:    - A's true direction is the arrow shown inside A.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:354:    - B's true direction is not its own shown arrow; it is sign(A_display - B_display).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:361:    legend directions must itself be decoded from the relationship between the two visible arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/13/code.py:40:#    The rule family is narrowed to symmetry transforms because that is the most\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/15/code.py:39:#    - The family is intentionally narrow: one validated landform, horizontal mirroring, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头图例+沿墙滑动\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:11:#      color itself forms a small arrow silhouette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:14:#    - Fusion rule used here: the arrow still has an orientation, but that orientation is not a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:16:#      the matching legend corner, the arrow tells us which of the two tangent directions to take\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:19:#    - Small trace: if a TL-corner legend contains a wall-colored arrow pointing east, then for\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:22:#      step is east, it uses the counterclockwise track. The same arrow would have meant \\\"slide\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:28:#    - Arrow directions still come from a small discrete family (4 cardinals via 5x5 arrows, 4\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:29:#      diagonals via 6x7 arrows), avoiding excessive freedom while keeping the visual cue obvious.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:35:#      That is invalid now because legends are two-color arrow templates. The new solver matches\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:36:#      the dominant-color silhouette against 5x5 / 6x7 arrow masks.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:42:#    - Fusion-specific new assumption: the arrow direction must equal one of the two possible first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:47:#      so later-chosen 5x5 or 6x7 arrows never collide with walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:54:#      the legend visibly looks like an arrow rather than a dot-offset code, and the yellows stay\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:56:#    - Because the arrow matches the initial tangent at the anchor, samples make clear that the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:57:#      arrow is not a free-space motion vector: the yellows do not cut across the room.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:68:#    - The chosen arrow direction equals the clockwise first step or the counterclockwise first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:135:def _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:140:def _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:152:CARDINAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRS}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:153:DIAGONAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in DIAGONAL_DIRS}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:164:        patch[_cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:167:    patch[_diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:207:def _match_arrow_direction(fill_mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:219:def _legend_arrow_info(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[int, int], str]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:221:    Detect border legends and decode wall_color -> (arrow_direction, corner).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:224:    silhouette against arrow templates instead of comparing minority-color centroids.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:243:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(patch == fill)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:360:def _select_track_from_arrow(profile: dict[str, object], arrow_dir: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:363:    if arrow_dir == cw_dir and arrow_dir != ccw_dir:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:365:    if arrow_dir == ccw_dir and arrow_dir != cw_dir:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:368:    cw_score = _dir_score(cw_dir, arrow_dir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:369:    ccw_score = _dir_score(ccw_dir, arrow_dir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:394:    Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions along the inner wall, using arrow legends as entry tangents.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:400:      region wall color, and that dominant color is arranged as a visible arrow silhouette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:405:    - The legend arrow does not mean \\\"move straight through the room\\\". Instead it selects which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:410:    Key insight: The legend color still links the correct room, but the arrow now chooses the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:417:    legend_info = _legend_arrow_info(g, bg)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:449:        arrow_dir, corner = legend_info[border_col]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:453:        track = _select_track_from_arrow(profile, arrow_dir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头图例+仅基数方向\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:13:#     - D1/0: 方向不再来自双色质心，而是来自 5x5 图例里由墙色 C 画出的粗箭头轮廓。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:17:#     - 融合后示例：若右上角图例是 5x5 两色矩形，墙色 C 在其中形成一个朝右的箭头，则 solver\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:22:#     - 箭头只保留 4 个取值，既能明显看出与原题不同，又避免 20x20 上出现难辨认的小对角模板。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:23:#     - 箭头模板采用粗短且不对称的 5x5 轮廓，降低与普通色块混淆的风险。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:26:#     - 新 solver 改为要求图例是边界上的 5x5 实心矩形、恰含两色，且主色掩码精确匹配四个箭头模板之一。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:34:#     - 人类可直接看到：角落小块里的墙色本身画成箭头，且黄色总是沿箭头所指的上下左右方向靠墙。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:35:#     - 没有对角运动，也没有依赖颜色编号的隐式排序；方向信息完全来自肉眼可见的箭头朝向。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:37:#     - 图例只有 \\\"墙色箭头 + 统一底板\\\" 两层信息，比原题三色点标更紧凑。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:42:#     - 量化验证时应统计：所有 legend 是否都是两色 5x5 箭头、方向是否覆盖 4 个基数档位，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:45:#     - 假设每个 legend 的主色掩码恰好等于四个 5x5 箭头模板之一；generator 会严格按模板构造。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:90:def _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:97:    patch[_cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:101:CARDINAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRS}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:116:def _match_arrow_direction(fill_mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:127:    Detect border legends and decode direction from a dominant-color 5x5 arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:130:    controls. The dominant-color cells form one of four cardinal arrow templates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:149:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(patch == fill)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:185:    Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions using border legends drawn as cardinal arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:191:      that forms a visible arrow shape, plus a uniform backing color. The wall color C matches the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:196:      find the legend whose dominant arrow color is also C.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:197:    - Read the arrow orientation directly as one of the four cardinal directions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/1/code.py:202:    from the legend's arrow silhouette itself, and every valid movement is purely horizontal or\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:3:# Name: 向量差解码+箭头图例\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:17:      drawn as a coarse arrow silhouette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:18:    - The visible arrow direction is the legend's displayed vector.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:22:    - Suppose the left legend uses color 7 and shows a right arrow, so display_left = (0, 1).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:23:    - Suppose the right legend uses color 5 and shows a down arrow, so display_right = (1, 0).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:24:    - In the source task or in the pure arrow-shape variant, color-5 rooms would slide down.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:28:        2. decode each rectangle's arrow shape into a displayed vector;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:37:  - The arrow silhouettes are intentionally chunky and asymmetric, so humans can read them\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:55:    3. the dominant legend-color mask matches one of the 5x5/6x7 arrow templates;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:65:  - Humans can first read the left arrow in the usual way, then compare it to the right arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:66:  - Right-colored rooms visibly disobey their own displayed arrow and instead follow the vector\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:79:  - Color 1 is just a legend plate color; all nontrivial inference comes from arrow orientation\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:83:  - Metric: compare the combo output against a legacy-arrow output that incorrectly lets the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:84:    second wall color follow its own displayed arrow directly.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:90:  - main() assumes the dominant legend color is the wall color; generator uses masks where the arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:171:def _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:176:def _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:188:CARDINAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRS}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:189:DIAGONAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in DIAGONAL_DIRS}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:194:    patch[_cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:200:    patch[_diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:210:def _match_arrow_direction(fill_mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:249:    direction = _match_arrow_direction(patch == fill_col)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:362:    Slide yellow pixels inside enclosed rooms using arrow legends plus a derived second instruction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:366:    - Two small legend rectangles sit on the top border. Each uses wall color C as a chunky arrow silhouette on a color-1 plate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:370:    - Decode each legend's displayed direction from the orientation of its wall-colored arrow shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:375:    first read arrow shapes as vectors, then derive the second color's true motion by vector subtraction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/14/code.py:33:      to a sign-only arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:24:#      original: two differently colored fenced rooms might use two different arrows, and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/44/code.py:41:#    - Original code accepted any grid size. This combo intentionally narrows the family to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:33:  方向语义仍完全来自 center->indicator 的质心符号，而不是颜色编号或硬编码箭头类别。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:21:#        forces the frontier to progress through a narrower lower path;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/10/code.py:38:      \\\"legend color picks the chamber, legend arrow gives one of four directions, the yellow bar\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/10/code.py:339:    Slide yellow rigid line segments inside closed wall regions using cardinal legend arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/10/code.py:356:    - The legend color still selects which arrow applies to which chamber, but the yellow object is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/9/code.py:16:#     The local water physics stays the same as the original task, but the admissible input family is narrowed to a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/19/code.py:320:    - The lower structure is one bottom-anchored chain of 4-5 narrow basins, while the input water starts\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/4/code.py:82:#       观察多个样例时，人类会看到：legend 箭头方向与 scattered source 旁 cue 的方向一一对应，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:16:#      A 只有细尾巴；B 同时有箭头头部且导线从其两侧穿过；C 只有终点箭头头部。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:46:#    - 中间带箭头且导线继续穿过的节点对应 bridge；\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:47:#    - 终点箭头对应 final target。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:259:    - No red/green marker bars remain. Instead, one control-color chain occupies the bottom two rows: a tail-only start node, a pass-through arrow node in the middle, and a terminal arrow node at the end.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:262:    - The tail-only lane is the source A, the middle pass-through arrow lane is the bridge B, and the terminal arrow lane is the final target C.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/37/code.py:65:    class narrow while still preventing a brittle \\\"exactly one shape\\\" shortcut.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/27/code.py:19:#    - D17/0 is narrowed by the fusion description: only the unmarked spectator lanes turn grey, rather than\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/28/code.py:76:#   center alignment is not explainable by simply following the legend arrow. This\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/12/code.py:96:#       This keeps the inference space narrow enough for ARC-style reasoning.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/17/code.py:34:   - Marker geometry is also narrow: a short 1xk or kx1 segment outside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:3:# Name: 统一轴向射线+形状决定距离+箭头精灵\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:21:#   - Every sprite is now a 3-pixel arrow that points directly along one of the 4 cardinal\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:24:#     encoded by arrow family:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:25:#       * kind \\\"L\\\": skew hook arrow, range 4\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:26:#       * kind \\\"V\\\": symmetric chevron arrow, range 6\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:29:#       * fused analogue can be a short-range up arrow {(5,5),(6,4),(6,5)}.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:31:#       * a long-range up arrow {(5,5),(6,4),(6,6)} points the same way but lands at\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:32:#         (-1,5) conceptually, so the generator only places such arrows where tip+6*dir stays\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:34:#         arrow silhouette plus the induced landing distance.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:36:#   - The fusion is not simplified into a single arrow template: there are two reusable shape\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:41:#   - Generator examples force both arrow families to appear and reject cases whose output is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:45:#     monochrome, 8-connected arrow matching exactly one template. The generator uses only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:46:#     those templates and validates them with _arrow_info(...).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:50:#     _arrow_info returns only those labels, and generator placements are precomputed by kind.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:54:#   - Placements are precomputed only when both the arrow cells and tip+range*dir destination\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:59:#   - All arrows are axis-aligned, so the D1 change is visible directly in the input.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:60:#   - The two arrow silhouettes are visually distinct, and both appear repeatedly, so the D2\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:66:#   - No rule depends on hidden ordering or color ranking; only local shape family, arrow tip,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:111:def _arrow_info(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:114:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (tip_rc, dir_rc, kind) for a 3-cell axis arrow sprite, else None.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:147:        info = _arrow_info(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:177:    Fire straight projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, with range determined by arrow family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:180:    - The background is the most common color, and each foreground component is a 3-cell monochrome arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:181:    - Every arrow points directly up, down, left, or right from a single tip cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:182:    - There are two arrow silhouettes: a skew hook family and a symmetric chevron family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:185:    - Read the firing direction from the arrow tip itself; all projectiles travel along cardinal rays only.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:186:    - The arrow family sets the distance: hook arrows (the former L-coded family) travel 4 cells, while chevron arrows (the former V-coded family) travel 6 cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:191:    - Direction has become visually explicit, so the remaining inference is to separate the two arrow families and notice that they keep different fixed ranges even though they shoot along the same four axes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:319:    return all(_arrow_info(comp) is not None for comp in comps)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/8/code.py:28:#    The topology family is still narrow enough that 2-4 examples support the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:33:       a left token drops through 6, while under the old narrow-gate rule it would have\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:39:     The generator therefore enforces at least two wide gates and at least two narrow gates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:42:     every wide gate as narrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:66:     bars, and the corresponding output rows show narrow vs wide opened passages around the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:68:   - Because accepted samples must differ from the \\\"all narrow\\\" baseline, the width signal is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:383:def _baseline_narrow_gates(gates: list[list[tuple[int, int]]]) -> list[list[tuple[int, int]]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:460:    baseline_opened = _build_opened_grid(_baseline_narrow_gates(gates), width)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:471:    enriched_stats[\\\"narrow_gates\\\"] = int(sum(span == NARROW for row in gates for _center, span in row))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:473:    enriched_stats[\\\"diff_vs_narrow\\\"] = int(np.count_nonzero(fused_out != baseline_out))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:496:    if int(stats[\\\"narrow_gates\\\"]) < 2:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:506:    if int(stats[\\\"diff_vs_narrow\\\"]) < 1:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:16:#      a pair of narrow lower shafts that can catch falling liquid. The fused palette is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:33:#    - The color freedom is intentionally narrow. Using exactly two fresh colors plus one old\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:36:#    - The geometry is also narrow: both fresh sources feed into two one-cell-wide shafts.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:71:#      narrow liquid shafts. No legends or overlapping annotations are added.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/27/code.py:75:  reasoning space narrow and readable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/22/code.py:40:#    - Original assumption: a gate row may have 0-3 gates. The combo narrows this to exactly one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/4/code.py:51:    column), which keeps the visual language narrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/20/code.py:58:#    narrow, so the output reads as maroon spread through many triangles plus a few\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/8/code.py:69:#     narrower rectangle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/16/code.py:55:#    - The crop is equally visible because outputs are narrower and shorter than the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/12/code.py:31:#    The layout family is intentionally narrow: three cups, one lower source roof, and only five\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:3:# Name: 图例顺序编码方向加箭头图例\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:37:#    The obstacle family stays narrow and readable: 3-4 solid edge bars, 2-4 cell\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:162:    arrow_patch = mask[_ARROW_ROWS, _ARROW_COLS]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:164:        if np.array_equal(arrow_patch, template):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:166:    raise AssertionError(f\\\"unrecognized legend arrow patch:\\\\n{arrow_patch.astype(int)}\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:292:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build the fixed 6x24 legend band using swatches plus mirrored elbow arrows.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:572:    Trace legend-ordered teal rays whose turn rules come from arrow glyphs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:595:    arrow glyph gives each obstacle color's turn direction, and the visible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/22/code.py:191:    - Process foreground colors in priority order by compactness: clean the narrow reference color first by the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头精灵+方向由最近边缘决定\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:18:#    The visible sprites are now 3-pixel arrows in 8 compass facings, so the input suggests\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:19:#    \\\"follow the arrow tip\\\". The fusion rule breaks that expectation: the tip still marks the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:22:#      cells {(3,6),(4,5),(4,6)} form a NE-looking arrow with tip (3,6).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:28:#      fires upward to an in-bounds cell even though the arrow still visually points NE.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:33:#    - Keep exactly 8 arrow templates and exactly 4 actual firing directions (toward top/bottom/\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:35:#    - Require both diagonal-looking and axis-looking arrows in each generated grid; otherwise the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:37:#    - Require repeated evidence that arrows are misleading: several sprites must fire in a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:43:#      combo, only emitter recovery survives, and it must be replaced by arrow-template matching.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:51:#    - Generation precomputes all arrow placements whose 3 cells are in bounds, whose nearest edge\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:55:#    - Under this toward-edge geometry, legal 5-step destinations stay in narrow border bands.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:61:#    - The crucial observable is disagreement between arrow facing and actual shot direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:63:#      arrow\\\" solver on the same input.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:65:#      arrow facings within at least one shared nearest-edge class.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:78:#    - For each sprite, compare `visual_dir` from the arrow template with `actual_dir` from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:84:#    - Every non-bg component is exactly one 3-pixel arrow matching a unique template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:85:#    - Every generated arrow has a unique nearest edge; ties are excluded.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:86:#    - The projectile always starts from the arrow tip, not from any other pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:138:def _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:175:def _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:180:    tip_data = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:193:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, but aim them by border proximity instead of arrow facing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:197:    - Every non-background 8-connected component is a monochrome 3-pixel arrow in one of 8 visual facings.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:198:    - The arrow tip still identifies the launch cell, but the arrow's pointing direction is not the movement rule.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:201:    - Match each component to an arrow template to recover its tip.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:206:    Key insight: The arrowhead is a red herring. Shape tells you where the shot starts, but the shot direction comes from the sprite's global position relative to the border.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:223:        td = _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(comp, h, w)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:267:        td = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:429:        if _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(coords, H, W) is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/31/code.py:64:  wide enough to be seen by eye, narrow enough that the frame grid still reads as one object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:255:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"图例顺序编码方向加箭头图例\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:448:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头图例双参数编码可变角度\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/36/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头图例双参数编码可变角度\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/36/code.py:10:      - replace each legend bar with a bottom-aligned colored hook / arrow token inside a 4x4 black cell\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/29/code.py:64:    Key insight: The separator spacing reveals the slot-grid dimensions, but the occupied extent of the top-band shapes reveals the narrower template width; marker locality and marker color must be decoded separately.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/24/code.py:80:    Key insight: Color still narrows the choice to a template group, but repeated colors are resolved by visible marker frequency, while the marker's local position still encodes the output block location.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/15/code.py:43:#   - The long-approach change is kept in a narrow range: obstacle md 5-12, mostly produced by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/18/code.py:478:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Carve a narrow background fjord from the left edge without disconnecting the path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:354:        raise ValueError(\\\"grid too narrow for dependency corridor\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:67:#     - Payload cells lie on a narrow ring around the cross, so the local geometry\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/1/code.py:544:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Carve a narrow bg separator from the left edge without disconnecting path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/21/code.py:40:#    - Object count is narrowed to exactly 4 (a 2x2 frame grid). This keeps the legend short and lets frame colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/11/code.py:66:#     To keep the task solvable, the generator narrows the rectangle size and piece\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:21:#   - Width is restricted to the small visible set {2, 3}; that is narrow enough\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:33:#     non-background population. The generator keeps the narrow band dominant over\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:481:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Stable 15x15 narrow-band layout with a readable left-edge separator.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头头部对准目标点\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:20:# - The head is no longer a full edge line. It is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:26:#   in the arrow's pointing direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:27:# - The translation distance is measured from the arrow tip to the point, not from arrow bbox\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:28:#   top-left and not from a full line center. After moving k steps, the arrow tip advances by k and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:33:#   D4/2 alone: an arrow attached on the left may still point down, so direction comes from shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:35:#   Combo here: an arrow attached orthogonally to the motion axis points toward a single dot, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:36:#   the arrow tip rather than any bbox anchor is what aligns to that dot.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:37:#   Example: a right-pointing arrow attached above the container has tip at (r, c). A point sits at\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:42:# - The arrow vocabulary is still only four shapes, keeping shape parsing low-entropy.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:43:# - To ensure this is visibly different from the source task, the generator only attaches arrows on\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:46:# - The target is always a point with at least one background cell between it and the arrow tip, so\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:51:#   Broken. In the combo, the arrow may be above the box while motion is right.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:55:#   top-left. Broken again: a point has no meaningful shared shape anchor with the arrow. The new\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:56:#   anchor is the arrow tip.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:58:#   between arrow tip and point. The solver still contains a tiny fallback for malformed gap=0\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:59:#   inputs by trying to peel one extra pixel off an otherwise valid arrow component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:62:# - Each generated assembly reserves the union of five regions: input container, input arrow,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:63:#   destination point, moved container, moved arrow. Packing is done with a 1-cell background moat.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:68:# - Across samples, the arrow is visibly not on the side of travel, forcing the solver to read its\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:73:# - Only three foreground object types appear: bordered container, arrow head, point target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:74:#   The point is sparse, the arrow is compact, and assemblies are separated by background.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:78:#   direction, so the only new inference burden is the fused geometry: arrow orientation + tip to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:82:# - Head components are exact 3x3 arrow sprites, or that sprite plus one fused forward point in the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:84:# - Every mover has exactly one nearest forward point on its arrow ray; the generator verifies\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:86:# - Motion direction, fill order, and point alignment are all keyed off the arrow direction, not\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:147:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:157:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:180:def _parse_arrow_component(pts: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> dict | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:226:    - The source marker is a 3x3 arrow sprite whose orientation gives the movement direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:228:    - Distance is measured from the arrow tip to the target point.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:290:        parsed = _parse_arrow_component(set(comp0[\\\"pts\\\"]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:422:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:531:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), s[\\\"direction\\\"], HEAD_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:563:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), s[\\\"direction\\\"], HEAD_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/21/code.py:29:#    The added freedom is intentionally narrow. There is still one shared direction, 3 or 5 segments, and one median\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/16/code.py:41:#   - Original assumption: frame sizes live in a narrow band. Broken here because large-vs-small frame\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头标记编码方向+L/T形模板\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:19:# - Fused task: the source is now a 3-cell arrowhead whose geometry fixes the first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:24:#   is read as [red, blue, yellow]. An up-pointing yellow arrow starts at yellow,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:28:# - Markers use only four unambiguous arrowhead shapes `> < ^ v`; this keeps the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:42:#   every decoded arrow tip must point to an ambient path cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:46:#   arrows remain separate 8-connected components.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:52:# - Humans can see two independent cues in the input: arrow orientation decides the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:54:# - The generator requires at least one arrow whose decoded heading differs from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:67:# - There are 1-2 arrow markers, each an 8-connected size-3 component matching\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:68:#   exactly one arrowhead orientation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:105:def _arrow_cells(tip_r: int, tip_c: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:109:def _decode_arrow_component(coords: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:110:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (tip_r, tip_c, direction) for a 3-cell arrowhead component.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:117:            if set(_arrow_cells(int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction)) == comp:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:182:def _find_arrow_markers(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:185:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Find 3-cell arrow markers whose colors belong to the decoded cycle.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:192:            decoded = _decode_arrow_component(coords)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:211:def _assert_arrow_markers_valid(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:217:    assert 1 <= len(markers) <= 2, f\\\"expected 1-2 arrow markers, got {len(markers)}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:221:        assert tuple(sorted(_arrow_cells(tip_r, tip_c, direction))) == cells, (\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:295:    - Start markers are 3-cell arrowheads in template colors, embedded inside the path region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:300:    - Each arrow launches one particle from its tip in the direction encoded by the arrowhead shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:304:    Key insight: The path dynamics are still the original alternating-turn walk, but the input now hides two independent controls in local geometry: arrow shape chooses the initial heading, and corner-template shape chooses the usable cycle order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:333:    markers = _find_arrow_markers(g, pattern, path_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:334:    _assert_arrow_markers_valid(g, markers, path_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:494:def _collect_arrow_candidates(mask: np.ndarray, target_row: int) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:508:                    cells = _arrow_cells(int(r), int(c), direction)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:547:def _place_arrow_markers(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:553:    cand_lists = [_collect_arrow_candidates(mask, int(row)) for row in target_rows]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:599:    # Right-pointing arrows are structurally rarer because they usually agree\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:601:    # legal pair containing one R arrow while still requiring another\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:602:    # interesting arrow, so D4 remains observable and direction branches stay covered.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:715:    placed = _place_arrow_markers(g, mask, target_rows, marker_colors)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/9/code.py:20:#   The family is intentionally narrow: one frame, 2 or 3 tools, strictly decreasing\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:3:# Name: 内部图案决定方向加箭头头部\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:21:# - Outside the container there is now a 3x3 maroon arrow head plus a matching\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:22:#   3x3 maroon destination arrow further along the travel direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:25:#     2. Use the external arrow only as the movable head sprite and as a visual\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:27:# - To make that visible, the head arrow is always attached on a side orthogonal\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:30:#     * internal orange cells form a right-pointing arrow template\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:31:#     * external arrow head also points right, but it is attached above or below\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:34:#       destination arrow to the right of the source arrow, then move container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:38:#     * fused: internal orange arrow decides direction, head position is decoupled\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:39:#       from direction, and the head itself is a compact arrow sprite\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:43:# - The internal cue is a fixed 4-cell arrow template, not an arbitrary shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:44:# - The external cue is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:53:#   still keep its identity. Broken: a 3x3 arrow must be tracked as a full shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:55:#   must depend on the internal arrow direction instead.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:56:# - New assumption introduced here: movers have a unique internal arrow template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:60:# - New assumption introduced here: the external arrow direction agrees with the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:61:#   internal arrow direction. Generator guarantees this and solver checks it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:65:#     input container, input head arrow, destination arrow,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:66:#     moved container, moved head arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:70:#   arrows from appearing between a source head and its own destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:76:# - The head arrow points the same way as the internal motif, acting as a second\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:81:# - Each assembly contains one container, one source arrow, one destination arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:83:#   head lands exactly on its destination arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:87:# - Orange growth is structurally tied to the same inferred direction: the arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:92:#   old same-side head as an arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:131:def _arrow_template(inner_h: int, inner_w: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:156:    base = _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:185:        template = set(_arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:193:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:203:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:233:    - Read direction from the internal orange arrow template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:234:    - The adjacent external 3x3 arrow is the movable head sprite, but its\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:236:    - Move container + head toward the nearest matching arrow destination along\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:370:    for r, c in _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:414:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:516:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), spec[\\\"direction\\\"], HEAD_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:517:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (dr, dc), spec[\\\"direction\\\"], HEAD_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:551:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), spec[\\\"direction\\\"], HEAD_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:289:    Recolor particles as they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/10/code.py:63:#    In the output the near group stays flat, the middle group becomes tall/narrow,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:185:def _narrow_vertical_corridor(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:432:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, jc, top1, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=5):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:435:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, right_root[1], top2, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=6):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:34:#      target. If a choke narrows below 6, the mover stops at the farthest\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:74:#    - Big mover sizes 5..7 make narrow gates visibly narrower than the mover.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:84:#      large mover footprint interacting with visibly narrow chokepoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:308:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, max(1, n - 2))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:309:    remove = int(n - narrow_w)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/28/code.py:390:      generated tasks connector color already narrows the candidate set, and the final validation\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_retest_20260516.json:241:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_retest_20260516.json:335:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_review_summary_20260516.json:210:      \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_review_summary_20260516.json:290:      \\\"name\\\": \\\"显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/3/code.py:43:# - The destination structure changes visibly: wide bottom bars become narrow side bars.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_final_summary_20260516.json:205:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_final_summary_20260516.json:285:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:36:#      n×n clearance test needed for gradual narrowing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:39:#      because the taper can create upstream slack before the true narrowing point.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:48:#    - The river remains pixel-connected in blocked cases because the narrow spine still links\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:51:#    - Humans can see the one-sided staircase narrowing near the target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:53:#      the narrowing; it stops noticeably earlier, roughly halfway along the usable route.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:3:# Name: 符号转向指令+箭头标记+模板方向符号\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:22:# - Replace the old single-pixel sources with 3-cell arrowheads in the first cycle\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:23:#   color. The arrow tip is the launch cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:27:# - Fusion choice for the D4/D11 tension: every arrowhead must point in the same\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:30:#   `v` arrowheads, motion starts downward; if the turn bars read [L,R,R], later\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:36:# - The added symbols all use low-cardinality, human-visible geometry: arrow shape,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:46:#   replaced by 8-connected size-3 arrowhead decoding.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:48:#   new symbolic cues, so the solver now decodes the arrowheads and template glyph\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:65:#   the paint cycle, side bars are the turn sequence, and the arrow/glyph direction\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:73:#   glyph stay in the top-left template region, while arrowheads stay inside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:81:#   has exactly one indicator, the glyph direction matches every arrow marker, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:82:#   all placed arrows are non-degenerate against legacy neighbor-priority launch.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:106:def _arrow_cells(tip_r: int, tip_c: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:113:def _decode_arrow_component(coords: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:120:            if set(_arrow_cells(int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction)) == comp:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:157:        f\\\"arrow direction {marker_dir} must agree with template glyph {global_dir}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:162:def _find_arrow_markers(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:170:        decoded = _decode_arrow_component(coords)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:189:def _assert_arrow_markers_valid(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:196:    assert 1 <= len(markers) <= 2, f\\\"expected 1-2 arrow markers, got {len(markers)}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:202:        assert tuple(sorted(_arrow_cells(tip_r, tip_c, direction))) == cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:310:    markers = _find_arrow_markers(g, int(pattern[0]), int(path_color))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:311:    _assert_arrow_markers_valid(g, markers, int(path_color), str(global_dir))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:441:    Simulate recoloring particles on a path using arrow-shaped sources plus template direction symbols.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:446:    - Start markers are 3-cell arrowheads in the first cycle color, embedded inside the path band, and a separate 2x2 block provides the terminal collision color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:450:    - Decode each arrow marker and require its pointing direction to agree with the template glyph; each particle starts from the arrow tip in that shared direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:455:    - The template now carries two independent symbolic programs at once: block colors specify the repaint cycle, and instruction marks specify both the shared launch heading and the collision-turn schedule, while the arrowheads localize the actual start tips and confirm the heading geometrically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:592:def _collect_arrow_candidates(mask: np.ndarray, target_row: int) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:605:                    cells = _arrow_cells(int(r), int(c), direction)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:638:def _place_arrow_markers(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:641:    cand_lists = [_collect_arrow_candidates(mask, int(row)) for row in target_rows]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:782:    placed = _place_arrow_markers(g, mask, target_rows, int(cycle_colors[0]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:91:- The occupied non-background area is constrained to 10-20% of the grid, matching the sparse-narrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/6/code.py:26:#     The final box is two cells narrower and the surviving interior contains two bg holes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:36:  otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable n×n placement before the first too-narrow gate\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:59:- Original assumption: a stuck case only comes from river self-narrowing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/29/code.py:162:    assert w >= 2, \\\"grid too narrow for legend\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/29/code.py:240:      colors themselves encode the slot's top-to-bottom order. Combining both signals narrows\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/30/code.py:56:#    Gap sizes remain in a narrow range so the board stays sparse and legible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:3:# Name: 显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:28:#   3. Reflection is read from arrow glyphs inside the matched target quadrant:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:29:#      right-arrow => LR flip, down-arrow => UD flip. Quadrant position no longer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:35:#     * connector + only down-arrow -> copy there, but apply UD instead of LR;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:36:#     * connector + both arrows -> copy there with both flips.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:59:#   arrows are instruction artifacts. They are stripped before motifs are stamped.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:66:#   regions are large enough for anchors, arrow glyphs, and at least one-cell\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:70:# - Active target anchors reserve a top band for arrows and at least one extra row\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:77:#   3. read the arrows in those same quadrants to decide the reflection bits.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:83:# - Colors are function-separated: divider=1, anchors=2, arrows=3, bg=4,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:97:#   quadrants with both a connector color repeated in TL and at least one arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:330:    Copy the TL motif into connector-matched regions, scaling by anchor size and mirroring by arrow markers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:335:    - Each active target shares a repeated connector color with a TL-side connector stub, and that same target region also contains one or two green arrow glyphs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:339:    - Extract the TL motif while ignoring connector colors, then for each active target read its arrows: right-arrow means LR reflection, down-arrow means UD reflection.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:342:    Key insight: The divider only tells you where the four regions are; connector colors decide which anchors participate at all, and arrow glyphs independently decide how each matched copy is reflected.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:561:def _paint_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, top: int, left: int, shape: frozenset[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:569:        _paint_arrow(grid, q_r0 + 1, q_c0 + 1, RIGHT_ARROW)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:571:        _paint_arrow(grid, q_r0 + 1, q_c0 + 5, DOWN_ARROW)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/2/code.py:59:    - B pieces are narrow rectangles placed far enough from the notch columns to avoid overlap inside bars\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:58:     colors, so the solver must detect the arrow-marked L component and the dock structurally.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:259:def _find_arrow_l_info(comp: dict) -> dict | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:371:        info = _find_arrow_l_info(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/25/code.py:95:#   long-left area-6 branch, so the walk grammar does not collapse to a narrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:17:     Each strip shows one glyph sample on the left and one 5x5 arrow exemplar on the right:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:71:   - The 5x11 legend strips use a blank spacer column between glyph sample and arrow sample, keeping\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:82:   - Legend colors are purely stylistic: all legend shapes share one color, while arrow colors only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:83:     help distinguish arrow exemplars visually.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:89:     shape-vs-arrow samples; generator uses exactly that layout.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:134:# Right-side legend layout: one 5x5 glyph sample + spacer + one 5x5 arrow sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:272:    raise AssertionError(f\\\"unrecognized legend arrow patch:\\\\n{mask}\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:281:        arrow_patch = right[r0 : r0 + 5, LEGEND_ARROW_C0 : LEGEND_ARROW_C0 + 5]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:285:        glyph_to_dir[glyph_id] = _decode_dir_patch(arrow_patch, bg)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:307:      shows a glyph sample and a 5x5 arrow sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:542:        arrow = np.asarray(_DIR_TEMPLATES[direction], dtype=int)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/26/code.py:546:        ] = arrow * int(LEGEND_ARROW_COLORS[direction])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:332:    - If the current target is blocked by a too-narrow branch, the mover stops at the reachable placement\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:451:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:452:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/32/code.py:19:  river narrows below n, the mover gets stuck before the chokepoint.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:28:  - Stuck case: a later corridor segment is narrowed below n, so BFS stops at\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:415:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:416:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/15/code.py:57:#      least two rectangles in both the narrow-band and wide-band groups.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:55:# - The rule space is intentionally narrow: exactly one component, one mask, and exactly 2 rounds.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/15/code.py:309:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/15/code.py:310:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/20/code.py:367:    - Each structure is a rotated nested comb: a tall outer cavity contains a narrower inner cavity, and the true teeth are spaced apart (`101` or `10101`).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:345:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:346:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/40/code.py:388:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/40/code.py:389:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/39/code.py:375:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/39/code.py:376:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/9/code.py:299:    - Rank those candidate red plugs from smaller area to larger area, rank sockets from narrower span to wider span, then dock them in that order; all traversed cells become black and every other red vanishes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:17:        arrow sample, so direction must be looked up from shape -> arrow, not hard-coded.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:65:   - The right side uses a fixed strip layout with one blank spacer column between shape and arrow,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:80:     3x3 shape patch at local cols 0..2 and a 3x3 arrow patch at local cols 4..6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:123:# Right-side legend layout: one 3x3 shape sample + spacer + one 3x3 arrow sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:207:        arrow_patch = right[r0 : r0 + 3, LEGEND_ARROW_C0 : LEGEND_ARROW_C0 + 3]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:211:        glyph_to_dir[glyph_id] = _decode_dir_patch(arrow_patch, bg)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:223:      glyph sample and a 3x3 arrow sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:450:        arrow_template = _DIR_TEMPLATES[glyph_to_dir[glyph_id]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:455:            arrow_template * int(_LEGEND_ARROW_COLORS[glyph_to_dir[glyph_id]])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/53/code.py:126:    assert w >= 2, \\\"grid too narrow for color legend\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:32:#       the last gravity-reachable placement above the first too-narrow slice.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:66:#       the last shaft becomes narrower row by row. In blocked examples the mover stops just above\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:67:#       the narrow segment while the red square remains below it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:77:#       gravity-like descent plus a monotone narrowing that eventually becomes too tight.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:226:      too narrow for the square.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:226:    Original sliding-square physics on a very sparse narrow river, followed by a tight crop\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:331:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:332:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/19/code.py:25:#   exercising the sequential-consumption rule beyond one narrow branch.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/9/code.py:409:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/9/code.py:410:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/4/code.py:39:      1) 同方向但错连接器，证明不能只看箭头；\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/10/code.py:19:#      the farthest reachable placement before a chokepoint narrower than n.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/37/code.py:416:    - The damaged corner cannot be located from \\\"blank space\\\" because the hole already contains plausible pixels. Opposite-corner symmetry narrows the answer to a pair, and the filled D5-style center supplies the extra anchor that reveals which corner needs repair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/20/code.py:165:    The answer is not found by global glyph identity. Color only narrows the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/31/code.py:16:#   output transform; it is a deliberately narrower, cleaner input family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/7/code.py:159:    - A narrow legend strip occupies the left edge. Each 3x3 legend glyph has one trigger color at its center plus a gray shape that specifies that color's ray behavior.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:32:#      combo: detect arrow-shaped mover -> read its tip direction -> read border control\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:37:#    - n is restricted to 2..4. This keeps the arrow decomposition legible and avoids\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:57:#    - Across examples, humans can see one arrowed object, one plain target square, one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:58:#      red boundary dot, and outputs that sometimes follow the arrow and sometimes defy it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:103:def _arrow_square_info(comp: dict) -> dict | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:261:        mover_info = _arrow_square_info(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:404:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:405:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:793:    arrow_step = control_step if agree else (decoy_step if control_step == main_step else main_step)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:795:    tip = _choose_tip_cell(grid, mover_r, mover_c, n, STEP_TO_NAME[arrow_step])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/8/code.py:40:#    - The scatter freedom stays narrow: inter-band gaps are only 6 or 7, and within-band\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/24/code.py:44:#    - The new freedom is deliberately narrow. Irregularity is only 0/1 jitter on one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:47:  - a later horizontal gate may narrow to height 2, so it still passes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:48:  - the final horizontal gate may narrow to height 1, so the 2-high token stops\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:53:  - horizontal and vertical narrowings test different rectangle dimensions\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:346:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:347:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/5/code.py:28:#        original task: the black square stops because the blue river narrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头源+标记配对+X形双线\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:17:#    - Combo task: each endpoint is replaced by a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2 corner is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:18:#      the tip, and the missing diagonal quadrant is the arrow's forward direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:19:#    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:20:#      non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color are one pair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:21:#    - For one pair, the two tips lie on a common 45-degree diagonal and the arrows face each\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:28:#      combo logic: blue arrows with tips at (2,2),(6,6), same red marker color, facing toward\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:40:#    - Original blue-pixel grouping by diagonal is invalid: each arrow contains an incidental\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:43:#      colors attached to arrow tips.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:50:#      2. every arrow tip has exactly one adjacent non-bg, non-blue, non-magenta marker;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:51:#      3. every marker color labels exactly two arrows;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:52:#      4. paired arrows lie on one diagonal and face each other;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:57:#    - Both arrow bodies, both X branches, markers, triggers, and emitted rays must stay in-bounds\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:69:#      2. repeated marker colors identify which distant arrows pair up;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:144:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:156:def _parse_arrow_component(comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:178:def _find_arrow_sources(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[dict]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:181:    arrows: list[dict] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:199:            parsed = _parse_arrow_component(comp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:203:            arrows.append({\\\"tip\\\": tip, \\\"direction\\\": direction, \\\"cells\\\": comp})\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:205:    arrows.sort(key=lambda item: item[\\\"tip\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:206:    return arrows\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:231:    assert dr != 0 and abs(dr) == abs(dc), \\\"paired arrow tips must share a diagonal\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:238:    raise AssertionError(\\\"paired arrows must face each other along their tip diagonal\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:265:    arrows = _find_arrow_sources(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:267:    for arrow in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:268:        tip = arrow[\\\"tip\\\"]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:277:        marker_groups.setdefault(markers[0], []).append(arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:376:    Read marked blue arrow pairs, expand each pair into an X, and emit magenta rays from triggers touched by either branch.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:379:    - The background is the most common color. Active blue objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows; the degree-2 corner is the tip and the missing diagonal quadrant gives the arrow's facing direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:380:    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color belong together.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:384:    - For every marker-matched arrow pair, use the two tips as the endpoints of a direct diagonal and verify that the arrows face each other along it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:389:    - The solution must combine three cues at once: arrow geometry tells you where the real endpoints are and which way they face, repeated marker colors tell you which two arrows form a pair, and each pair generates an entire X so triggers can activate from either branch.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:397:    arrows = _find_arrow_sources(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:398:    assert arrows, \\\"grid must contain at least one valid blue arrow source\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:401:    for arrow in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:402:        tip = arrow[\\\"tip\\\"]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:411:        assert len(markers) == 1, \\\"each arrow tip must have exactly one adjacent marker\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:412:        marker_groups.setdefault(markers[0][2], []).append(arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:426:        assert len(group) == 2, \\\"each marker color must label exactly two arrows\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:517:        p_cells = _arrow_cells(p, direction)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:518:        q_cells = _arrow_cells(q, (-dr, -dc))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:519:        pair_arrow_cells = p_cells | q_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:520:        if any(not (0 <= r < h and 0 <= c < w) for r, c in pair_arrow_cells):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:522:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn for cell in pair_arrow_cells):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:527:        for cell in pair_arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:558:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn or cell in pair_arrow_cells for cell in ray_cells):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:563:        pair_blue_cells = blue_occupied | pair_arrow_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:564:        forbidden = occupied | drawn | path_cells | ray_cells | pair_arrow_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:577:            \\\"arrow_cells\\\": (p_cells, q_cells),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:610:        p_cells, q_cells = pair[\\\"arrow_cells\\\"]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:632:        p_cells, q_cells = pair[\\\"arrow_cells\\\"]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/_final_summary_20260517.json:62:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头源+标记配对\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/_final_summary_20260517.json:166:    \\\"name\\\": \\\"箭头源+标记配对+X形双线\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:33:#      combo task: one later spiral step is narrowed below width n, so the next spiral cell becomes infeasible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:46:#    - Width variation is limited to a few one-cell bulges and one optional narrowing gate. That is enough to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:62:#    - The narrowing gate only erases part of the leading row/column of the next spiral placement, preserving\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:67:#    - Reachable vs stuck examples differ by a visible local narrowing on a later ring or turn. The side bulge\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:32:     real chokepoint narrower than n and the mover always halts upstream.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:75:  human to infer \\\"the river gets erased behind the sliding block until the first too-narrow gate.\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:383:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:384:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:26:#   1. one green arrow glyph placed near the target anchor,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:28:# - The arrow gives the mandatory \\\"primary\\\" reflection:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:29:#     right arrow  -> LR reflection is required,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:30:#     down arrow   -> UD reflection is required.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:32:#   also needed. Concretely, after reading the arrow, the solver compares the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:38:#     1. read the local arrow; if it is a down arrow, start from UD instead,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:42:#   Difference: quadrant position no longer selects the mirror; the arrow gives\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:46:# - The arrow vocabulary stays tiny: exactly two 3x3 glyphs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:49:#   arrows alone are insufficient, and anchors alone are ambiguous without first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:50:#   knowing which primary axis the arrow selected.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:60:#   must remove arrow markers before stamping or they would leak into the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:62:#   arrows exist only outside TL, and the TL motif remains one 4-connected\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:66:# - The right arrow is drawn 1 cell above the anchor; the down arrow is drawn 1\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:71:# - The arrow is kept disconnected from the anchor, so component extraction for\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:75:# - A human can read the arrow as the obvious first instruction, then notice\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:76:#   that two targets with the same arrow can still differ because of the anchor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:78:# - The generator enforces both arrow types, both anchor states, and at least\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:82:# - Green is reserved for arrows and never used inside the motif.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:84:#   anchor, while arrows sit outside with a one-cell gap. This avoids overlap and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:88:# - No hidden color ordering is used. Red still marks anchors, green means arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:91:#   \\\"arrows only\\\" or \\\"original quadrant rule\\\" at the whole-output level.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:95:# - Every non-TL quadrant has exactly one arrow glyph and exactly one decorated\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:97:# - Each target anchor matches exactly one of two templates once its arrow-chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:212:def _read_arrow_primaries(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:225:        assert key != (0, 0), \\\"arrows are only allowed in non-TL quadrants\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:226:        assert key not in primaries, \\\"each non-TL quadrant must contain exactly one arrow glyph\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:229:            raise AssertionError(\\\"unrecognized arrow glyph\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:233:        assert key in primaries, \\\"each non-TL quadrant must contain exactly one arrow glyph\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:254:    Replicate the TL motif across quadrants with size scaling, arrow-selected primary reflection, and anchor-selected extra reflection.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:259:    - Each non-TL quadrant contains one decorated red anchor plus exactly one nearby green arrow glyph; the anchor size still varies by quadrant.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:263:    - In each target quadrant, read the arrow first to get the mandatory reflection axis: right arrow means LR, down arrow means UD.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:264:    - Compare the observed target-anchor template against the TL anchor under either that primary flip alone or both flips; apply the matching transform to the full source motif, scale by anchor-size ratio, align the red region to the target anchor, and stamp non-background pixels. Remove the green arrows from the final output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:266:    Key insight: The arrow does not fully specify the transform by itself. It only chooses the primary axis; the anchor's internal asymmetry tells you whether an additional orthogonal flip must be composed on top of it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:275:    primaries, marker_components = _read_arrow_primaries(g, mid_r, mid_c)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:515:def _paint_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, top: int, left: int, shape: frozenset[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:520:def _place_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, anchor_r: int, anchor_c: int, primary: tuple[bool, bool]) -> None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:523:        _paint_arrow(grid, anchor_r - 4, anchor_c, shape)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:525:        _paint_arrow(grid, anchor_r, anchor_c - 4, shape)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:611:    arrow_only_out = _build_output(patch, anchor_patch, tl_r0, tl_c0, target_sizes, anchors, primaries)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:613:    if int(np.count_nonzero(out != arrow_only_out)) < MIN_VARIANT_DIFF:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:624:        _place_arrow(inp, ar, ac, primaries[key])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:627:    # it is the reason arrow_only_out differs from out.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:59:#    - The legend is confined to a narrow corner strip with blank separator rows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:518:    use_narrow_hint = (n == 1 and random.random() < 0.75) or (n >= 2 and not reached)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:617:    if use_narrow_hint and cut_idx is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:400:    use_narrow_hint = (n == 1 and random.random() < 0.75) or (n >= 2 and not reached)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:489:    if use_narrow_hint:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:523:        if use_narrow_hint and not geo_ok:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:525:        if not use_narrow_hint and geo_ok != dest_ok:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:71:#     The corridor/background inversion is inferable from large-area corners vs narrow strip.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:319:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:320:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/13/code.py:265:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/13/code.py:266:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:12:#   or at the farthest reachable interior placement before a narrow gate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:51:#   examples, it stops inside just before a narrow section. No overlapping markers or\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:296:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:297:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/27/code.py:359:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample many near-sized areas from a narrow band.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:293:    - Magenta walls form narrow corridors near the destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/23/code.py:337:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/23/code.py:338:    remove = n - narrow_w\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/41/code.py:52:  - original blocker source: river narrows below width n,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:349:    - Each activated blob launches a ray from its uniquely narrowest extreme side, with width 1 or 2 from that side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头源+标记配对\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:18:#    - In this combo, each active source endpoint becomes a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:19:#      corner is the tip; the missing quadrant is the arrow's forward diagonal direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:20:#    - Each arrow also has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:21:#      non-magenta color. Marker colors are the pairing labels: two arrows with the same marker\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:22:#      color form one active pair. The segment is drawn between their tips, and both arrows must\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:24:#    - Example: suppose arrows A and B have red markers. A's tip is at (3,3) and points SE;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:26:#      inside the arrow bodies and could not tell which blue cells are endpoints. New logic first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:27:#      parses each 4-connected 3-cell L, extracts its tip/direction, groups arrows by marker\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:31:#      arrow distractor on the same diagonal extension as a real pair. Geometry-only pairing would\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:40:#    - At most one uniquely marked distractor arrow is added. That is enough to make marker-based\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:44:#    - The old `by_color[line_color]` pool is invalid because a single arrow contains three blue\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:51:#      3-cell L arrow, each such arrow must have exactly one adjacent marker, active marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:52:#      must appear on exactly two arrows, and those two arrows must face each other along a shared\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:59:#      distractor arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:60:#    - Marker cells are attached to the tip side of an arrow, stay off all active diagonals and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:61:#      future rays, and touch only their own arrow in 4-neighborhood.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:63:#      arrow unambiguously.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:66:#    - Humans can directly see the L-arrow cue and infer that the diagonal leaves the tip through\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:68:#    - Repeated marker colors across distant arrows make the pairing label visible in a few\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:71:#      then connect arrow tips\\\" is more plausible than any accidental one-off geometry heuristic.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:76:#    - Markers sit beside arrow tips instead of on the diagonal itself, so arrows, labels, path\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:78:#    - Distractor arrows, when present, are placed on diagonal extensions outside the active\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:82:#    - Marker colors do not transform into output colors; they only label which arrows belong\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:123:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:157:def _find_arrows(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> list[dict]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:160:    arrows: list[dict] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:206:            assert len(marker_cells) == 1, \\\"each arrow must have exactly one adjacent marker\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:208:            arrows.append(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:218:    arrows.sort(key=lambda a: (a[\\\"tip\\\"], a[\\\"marker_color\\\"]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:219:    return arrows\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:235:def _active_pairs_from_arrows(arrows: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:237:    for arrow in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:238:        marker_groups.setdefault(arrow[\\\"marker_color\\\"], []).append(arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:248:        assert ordered is not None, \\\"same-color arrow pair must be diagonal and face inward\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:265:    Read marked blue arrow sprites as diagonal endpoints, connect same-marked arrow pairs, then emit rays from magenta cells on those diagonals.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:268:    - bg = most common color. Blue source objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows whose corner cell is the tip and whose missing quadrant gives the forward diagonal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:269:    - Each arrow has one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Marker colors that appear twice define the active arrow pairs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:270:    - Magenta trigger cells may lie on the interior of active diagonals; uniquely marked arrows or off-diagonal magenta cells can appear as distractors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:273:    - Parse every valid blue arrow, group arrows by marker color, and for each marker color that labels exactly two arrows, draw the blue diagonal segment between their tips.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:277:    - Neither raw blue geometry nor marker colors alone are sufficient: the L-shape identifies the true tip and diagonal direction, while the repeated marker color decides which two arrows should actually be connected.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:285:    arrows = _find_arrows(grid, bg)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:286:    assert arrows, \\\"grid must contain at least one valid blue arrow\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:289:    for pair in _active_pairs_from_arrows(arrows):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:403:    Ablation: parse arrows but ignore marker colors, pairing each arrow with its farthest\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:410:    arrows = _find_arrows(grid, bg)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:413:    arrows_by_tip = {arrow[\\\"tip\\\"]: arrow for arrow in arrows}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:415:    for arrow in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:418:        for other in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:419:            if other is arrow:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:421:            ordered = _ordered_pair(arrow, other)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:424:            dist = abs(other[\\\"tip\\\"][0] - arrow[\\\"tip\\\"][0])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:429:            pair = tuple(sorted((arrow[\\\"tip\\\"], best_tip)))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:434:        left = arrows_by_tip[p]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:435:        right = arrows_by_tip[q]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:490:        start_cells = _arrow_cells(start, start_dir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:491:        end_cells = _arrow_cells(end, end_dir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:492:        all_arrow_cells = start_cells | end_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:495:        if any(not _in_bounds(h, w, cell) for cell in all_arrow_cells):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:497:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn for cell in all_arrow_cells | path_interior):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:499:        if any(cell in blue_occupied for cell in all_arrow_cells):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:501:        if any(nbr in blue_occupied for cell in all_arrow_cells for nbr in _neighbors4(*cell)):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:509:            \\\"arrows\\\": [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:540:def _try_place_decoy_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:566:        cells = _arrow_cells(tip, direction)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:620:        temp_blue = blue_occupied | placed[\\\"arrows\\\"][0][\\\"cells\\\"] | placed[\\\"arrows\\\"][1][\\\"cells\\\"]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:621:        for arrow in placed[\\\"arrows\\\"]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:622:            marker_cell = _find_marker_cell(arrow[\\\"tip\\\"], arrow[\\\"direction\\\"], h, w, temp_occupied, drawn | ray_cells | future_drawn, temp_blue)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:636:        for arrow in placed[\\\"arrows\\\"]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:637:            occupied.update(arrow[\\\"cells\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:638:            blue_occupied.update(arrow[\\\"cells\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:656:        placed = _try_place_decoy_arrow(segment, h, w, occupied, blue_occupied, drawn)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:676:        for arrow, marker_cell in zip(seg[\\\"arrows\\\"], seg[\\\"marker_cells\\\"]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:677:            for r, c in arrow[\\\"cells\\\"]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:697:            if any(abs(r - arrow[\\\"tip\\\"][0]) + abs(c - arrow[\\\"tip\\\"][1]) == 1 for seg in segments for arrow in seg[\\\"arrows\\\"]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:164:        raise AssertionError(\\\"vertical cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:183:    raise AssertionError(\\\"horizontal cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:188:    Build a red ray network by activating single-axis cross blobs whose narrowest arm is a hidden port.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:196:    - The activated cross then emits a ray from the uniquely narrowest arm tip, with width 1 or 2 depending on that arm.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:199:    Key insight: Direction is encoded geometrically, not by color. The only arm end that is strictly narrower than the other three extremes is the implicit launch port.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:334:# - a constant narrow top arm (width 1 or 2),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/29/code.py:190:      narrow arm tip. One marker ray may already be fully pre-expanded as an example.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/21/code.py:38:# - 不增加文字、箭头或标记层；对象仍是标准 ARC 块状轮廓。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/30/code.py:26:#    The fusion matters because D12 narrows the motif space to a recognizable typed vocabulary, while D3\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:28:  colors, so color only narrows the search to a group; it does not identify the true `dst`\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/3/code.py:292:        raise ValueError(\\\"bar side too narrow for sampled separator gap\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头精灵大瓦片颜色循环\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:18:#    - Anchor cue: the big monochrome objects are now rotated arrow sprites.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:25:#    Example: if a right-pointing arrow carries a 3x2 seed on its lower flank,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:30:#    The variant would become ambiguous if arrow directions, seed sizes, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:33:#    - one arrow template family,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:37:#    Seeds still differ by internal texture and arrow orientation, so the combo\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:42:#      clockwise flank, orthogonal to the ray. We must recognize arrow shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:45:#      origin from the matched arrow geometry plus a globally inferred tile size.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:50:#      color by exact arrow-shape matches.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:53:#    The generator is output-first. It places arrows with one-cell guard bands,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:55:#    any previous non-background payload. This guarantees that each arrow has\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:56:#    exactly one adjacent non-arrow component and label-based extraction stays\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:61:#    shows all three cues: the arrow points one way while the seed sits on a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:63:#    the same geometry but cycle their colors. Other arrows reuse the same size\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:68:#    other, and each grid uses only 2-4 arrows. This prevents component merges\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:79:#    - every sample uses at least two arrow orientations,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:85:#    - All arrows share one of the known templates, up to rotation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:87:#    - Exactly one adjacent marker component per arrow is present.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:196:def _oriented_arrow_spec(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:206:def _match_arrow_component(mask: np.ndarray) -> dict | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:210:            rotated, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:221:def _detect_arrow_color(grid: np.ndarray, *, bg: int) -> int | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:235:            if _match_arrow_component(local) is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:399:    Extend large marker tiles from arrow anchors, cycling colors on every repeated chunk.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:403:    - One non-background color forms several rotated arrow sprites from a small fixed template family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:404:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent large rectangular seed marker on a side flank, and exactly one arrow in the grid keeps its full long ray as the clue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:407:    - Read each arrow's pointing direction from its silhouette rather than from the marker attachment side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:408:    - Infer the shared seed-tile size from the compact markers, reconstruct the clue arrow's first tile, and learn a global color permutation by comparing consecutive full chunks on the long clue ray.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:409:    - For every arrow, repeat its seed rectangle outward in the arrow direction until the boundary, applying one more step of the learned color cycle after each whole-tile advance; arrow pixels are never overwritten.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:412:    The task now fuses three cues: arrow shape gives direction, the payload is a large textured rectangle, and the single long example ray reveals that repetition preserves geometry but rotates colors through a fixed global cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:419:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:420:    if arrow_color is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:423:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:424:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:428:    arrow_records: list[dict] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:431:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:432:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:433:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:436:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:437:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0) : int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0) : int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:438:        matched = _match_arrow_component(local_arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:443:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:467:        arrow_records.append(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:475:    if not arrow_records:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:484:    for record in arrow_records:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:501:        if np.any(tile == int(bg)) or np.any(tile == int(arrow_color)):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:527:            protect={int(arrow_color)},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:680:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:691:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:694:    arrow_color: int,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:699:    patch, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:711:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:712:        if not _cells_clear(arrow_cells, occ, arrow_guard, payload_guard):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:727:        if not _cells_clear(payload_cells, occ, arrow_guard, payload_guard):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:730:        for r, c in arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:732:            out[int(r), int(c)] = int(arrow_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:733:        _mark_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:758:    arrows: list[dict],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:762:    keep_idx = next(i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if bool(meta[\\\"is_clue\\\"]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:763:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:789:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:790:    if arrow_color is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:793:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:794:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:800:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:801:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:802:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:804:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:805:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0) : int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0) : int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:806:        matched = _match_arrow_component(local_arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:810:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:861:            protect={int(arrow_color)},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:874:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:875:    cycle_colors = list(map(int, rng.choice([c for c in others if int(c) != int(arrow_color)], size=_CYCLE_LEN, replace=False)))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:891:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:894:    arrows: list[dict] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:896:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:907:            arrow_guard=arrow_guard,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:910:            arrow_color=int(arrow_color),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:915:        arrows.append(meta)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:917:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, int(bg))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:77:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(-2, 0)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-2, -1), (-2, 1)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:85:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(-4, 0)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-4, -1), (-4, 1)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:97:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(0, 2)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-1, 2), (1, 2)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:105:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(0, 4)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-1, 4), (1, 4)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:117:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(2, 0)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(2, -1), (2, 1)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:125:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(4, 0)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(4, -1), (4, 1)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:137:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(0, -2)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-1, -2), (1, -2)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:145:                \\\"narrow\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": [(0, -4)], \\\"flanks\\\": [(-1, -4), (1, -4)], \\\"width\\\": 1},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:51:#    Yellow and teal are confined to narrow corridors outside the destination. Teal overrides yellow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:30:#    This makes the combo visually distinct from the original narrow markers without\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:5:# Name: 螺旋射线+箭头形起始标记\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:20:#    - New start object: a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite. Four red body pixels make the shaft/wedge and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:21:#      one yellow pixel protrudes on the firing side. The arrow tail is anchored on the boundary\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:29:#    - Example sketch: if a right-pointing arrow starts near the left edge, the first leg goes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:35:#    - Direction freedom is limited to the four cardinals and one arrow family, so the start cue is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:44:#      above it. That is false now, so start detection must match the arrow geometry instead.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:51:#    - New solver assumption: exactly one arrow exists; its red body has area 4; it has exactly one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:55:#    - Objects are still placed output-first. The generator paints the arrow, then for each active\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:62:#    - The arrow makes the initial direction visible without reading color ids. Horizontal starts\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:76:#      \\\"read direction from the arrow, then follow repeated clockwise turns.\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:95:# --- Start arrow ---\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:579:    Build a red activation network whose first launch comes from a small arrow and whose rays curl clockwise into spirals.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:584:    - The start marker is no longer a bottom stem; it is a boundary-anchored red arrow sprite with one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:588:    - Recolor the whole start arrow red, then launch a ray from the yellow tip in the direction implied\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:589:      by the arrow shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:597:    - Two cues must be read together: the arrow geometry gives the initial direction, and the repeated\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:604:    # --- STEP 1) Detect the start arrow sprite and infer the initial direction ---\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:694:    # --- STEP 5) Trace the arrow-launched spiral until it hits a blob or exhausts itself ---\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:732:    # Place the directional start arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:28:#    a single memorized picture, but the family stays narrow enough to remain\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:50:#    narrower and top-cropped relative to the input. A human can therefore infer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/24/code.py:43:#    The design is intentionally narrow instead of fully free-form:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/45/code.py:22:#     arm_len: generator keeps equal cardinal arms, but narrows the visible regime to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/45/code.py:344:# The generator intentionally narrows the arm/size regime to compact boards where\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:14:#     - After solving on the full canvas, the output is cropped to the narrow strip containing the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:128:    - After reconstructing the full solved canvas, keep only the narrow strip that contains the crosshairs and solved sprites.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/23/code.py:61:    Detect embedded '+' motifs inside a narrow strip and recolor each one to teal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/23/code.py:66:    - The true '+' motifs are arranged on one shared row or one shared column, so they read as a narrow 1-D chain, while other foreground cells are only distractors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:203:    - Magenta walls carve the board into a narrow maze.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/26/code.py:82:#   - Human solvers can compare narrow vs wide frames and see that one dot centers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/37/code.py:42:#    is visible in the output as wider or narrower rectangular corridors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7666fa5d/8/code.py:38:     by earlier, narrower stages.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:26:#          carve long narrow chambers rather than roughly square rooms.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:36:#      component, orthogonal rooms, and a small number of narrow chokepoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:48:#      narrow doorway would be mistaken for a real passage and the maze would\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:41:  The fused rule instead gives the narrow upper red frame two dots at its legal width-7\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:44:  frame color narrows candidates, spatial proximity resolves shared colors, and frame width\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:92:  differs between narrow and wide frames.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:37:#      usually horizontal only: blank outer columns disappear, producing a narrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:50:#    - To keep the change legible, generator columns come from two narrow but\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头形精灵凸出方向\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:15:# - This combo replaces the source object with arrow-shaped anchors and simultaneously changes the direction cue:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:16:#   the ray must follow the arrow's protruding head, not the side where the seed happens to touch.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:18:#   Example: a right-facing arrow may have its seed above or below it, but the output still repeats that seed to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:24:# - Each grid uses at least two arrow orientations, so the shape cue is actually demonstrated inside one sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:26:# - `detect_dominant_big_component_color()` still works because arrows remain the only components with bbox >= 3x3.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:31:# - The generator is output-first: place full arrows and full rays first, then erase all but one long clue ray.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:32:# - Arrows, rays, and their 4-neighborhood guards are kept separate so two non-arrow components never merge under\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:33:#   `label_mask((grid != bg) & (grid != arrow_color))`.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:34:# - Candidate seeds are rejected if they go out of bounds, overlap, or even touch previously committed rays / arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:36:# - The crucial cue is human-visible geometry: each arrow has one protruding tip and that tip points the repetition.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:38:# - The kept pre-extended clue ray shows that the repeated payload follows the arrow orientation rather than contact.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:41:# - No ray is allowed to touch a foreign arrow or another ray, so each object stays visually isolated.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:44:# - No ordering on color ids is used. Colors only separate background / arrow anchors / payload tiles.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:47:# - For every generated arrow, the attachment side should be orthogonal to the true ray direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:50:# - Solver assumes each big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template below.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:51:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-arrow component (seed or pre-extended ray component).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:215:def _build_arrow_lookup() -> dict[tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:224:_ARROW_LOOKUP = _build_arrow_lookup()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:227:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:254:def detect_arrow_component_color(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:260:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Choose the color whose big components best match the arrow template family.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:283:            if _match_arrow_direction(local) is not None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:295:# Extend marker rays from arrow-shaped anchors using the arrow head as the only direction cue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:298:# - One dominant non-background color forms several arrow sprites, all drawn from the same small template family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:299:# - Each arrow touches exactly one colored marker component, and exactly one of those components may already be a long\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:302:# - Recognize the arrow's facing direction from its protruding tip, not from the marker's contact side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:304:# - Repeat that tile from its current seed position all the way to the boundary in the arrow-indicated direction,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:305:#   while preserving arrow-colored cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:308:#   fails. Only the arrow silhouette's asymmetric protrusion consistently identifies the ray direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:315:    arrow_col = detect_arrow_component_color(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:316:    if arrow_col is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:319:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_col), connectivity=4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:320:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_col))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:324:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:325:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:326:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:329:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:330:        local_arrow = arrow_mask[int(ar0):int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0):int(ac1) + 1]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:331:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(local_arrow)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:336:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:362:            protect={int(arrow_col)},\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:543:def _cells_clear_for_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:546:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:550:        if int(occ[r, c]) != 0 or bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:558:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:560:    own_arrow: set[tuple[int, int]],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:563:        if (int(r), int(c)) in own_arrow:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:567:        if bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:572:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:580:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:583:    arrow_color: int,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:593:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:594:        if not _cells_clear_for_arrow(arrow_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:612:            own_arrow = set((int(r), int(c)) for r, c in arrow_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:613:            if not _cells_clear_for_ray(ray_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard, own_arrow):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:616:            for rr, cc in arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:618:                out[rr, cc] = int(arrow_color)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:619:            _mark_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:641:    arrows: list[dict],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:645:    pre_idx = max(range(len(arrows)), key=lambda i: arrows[i][\\\"tiles\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:646:    if arrows[pre_idx][\\\"tiles\\\"] < _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:647:        candidates = [i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if meta[\\\"tiles\\\"] >= _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:652:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:666:        raise ValueError(f\\\"unsupported arrow count: {n}\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:691:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:692:    palette = [c for c in others if c != arrow_color]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:700:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:703:    arrows: list[dict] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:705:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:713:            arrow_guard,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:716:            arrow_color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:720:        arrows.append(meta)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:722:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, bg, rng)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/17/code.py:31:#   and the cropped fill stays in a narrow range, making the edge-stop + tight\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/18/code.py:27:#        narrowed interval, stop before painting the stripe;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/18/code.py:30:#      - gap line: if the original input has foreground inside the current narrowed interval,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:9:#   inside the original segment span. Originally, yellow stripes are narrow span-only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:10:#   marks, while green stripes are narrow but also flood the full row/column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:191:    - yellow stripes keep the original narrow segment span but flood the full row/col\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:28:#    The family is kept narrow on purpose: a vertical backbone crosses two horizontal lines, which is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头编码方向+标记修正方向\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:46:#    replaces that with one yellow edge-L arrow plus one colored corner marker.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:47:#    The arrow has two perpendicular arms that already encode an ordered pair of candidate\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:48:#    directions: the longer arm is the arrow's direct direction, and the shorter arm is exactly\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:49:#    the clockwise-rotated alternative. Example: a top-edge arrow with elbow at (0, 6), long\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:55:#    on row 0 and later stripes appear on rows 2, 4, ... . The source arrow therefore matters\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:59:#    visible lengths and the longer arm is forced to be unique. That keeps the \\\"arrow points by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:68:#      direction. Now the edge only says \\\"the arrow is on this side\\\"; the actual direction comes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:73:#    - exactly one salient yellow component is the arrow source\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:79:#    The generator chooses one of eight edge templates so the arrow fits fully in-bounds, keeps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:81:#    corner marker only after the arrow is fixed. Interior blobs are placed with padded free\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:82:#    placement on a canvas that already contains the arrow and marker, so blobs cannot overlap\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:86:#    starting source is now visibly an arrow-like L rather than a plain segment. Comparing a few\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:88:#    arrow's long arm or its clockwise-rotated shorter arm. Because the two candidate outputs\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:92:#    `main()` assumes `_extract_arrow()` finds a single largest yellow L and that its shorter arm\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:98:#    contiguous row-span or col-span; the generator's arrow is made from straight runs, so that\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:145:def _extract_arrow(g: np.ndarray) -> dict[str, object] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:202:    arrow: dict[str, object],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:208:    elbow_r, elbow_c = (int(v) for v in arrow[\\\"elbow\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:211:        move_dir = str(arrow[\\\"rot_dir\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:212:        span_arm = list(arrow[\\\"base_arm\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:214:        move_dir = str(arrow[\\\"base_dir\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:215:        span_arm = list(arrow[\\\"rot_arm\\\"])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:283:    arrow = _extract_arrow(g)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:284:    if arrow is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:286:    return _paint_pattern(g, bg, _layout(arrow, g.shape, rotated=rotated))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:291:    Propagate the original Y,Y,G stripe process, but decode direction from a yellow edge-L arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:321:    arrow = _extract_arrow(g)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:322:    if arrow is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:331:    actual_layout = _layout(arrow, g.shape, rotated=rotated)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:333:        \\\"base_dir\\\": str(arrow[\\\"base_dir\\\"]),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:334:        \\\"rot_dir\\\": str(arrow[\\\"rot_dir\\\"]),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:336:        \\\"base_len\\\": int(arrow[\\\"base_len\\\"]),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:337:        \\\"rot_len\\\": int(arrow[\\\"rot_len\\\"]),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:345:def _paint_arrow(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:363:def _sample_arrow_spec(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:454:    spec = _sample_arrow_spec(rng, H, W)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:460:    _paint_arrow(grid, elbow=elbow, base_dir=base_dir, base_len=base_len, rot_len=rot_len)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:521:    arrow = _extract_arrow(canvas)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:522:    if arrow is None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:525:    layout = _layout(arrow, canvas.shape, rotated=rotated)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:3:# Name: 固定步数终止+箭头编码额外信息\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:30:    4 像素箭头 = 1 个额外像素（可加长竖臂或横臂） -> 固定走 5 步\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:31:    5 像素箭头 = 2 个额外像素（双臂都加长）       -> 固定走 8 步\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:34:    若箭头朝右下，起点是 S=(8,8)。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:43:- 4 像素箭头允许两种外观（延长竖臂或横臂），但语义相同。这提供少量形状变化而不增加推理分支。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:45:- 每个样例生成 3-4 个箭头，并强制同时出现 4 像素与 5 像素两类，使观察者能横向比较。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:49:- 原 `is_arrow_pts()` 假设箭头恒为 3 像素、bbox 恒为 2x2。这里不成立，必须改成模板匹配：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:51:- 原 `arrow_dir_and_start()` 用度数最大点找直角顶点；5 像素双延长时会出现多个度数相同候选。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:56:- 原 `wall_cells = non-bg - arrow_cells` 仍然可用，因为这次没有额外 tail 标记；但这要求墙颜色不能和箭头\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:57:  在 4 邻接上并成同色大连通块。generator 用箭头色/墙色分池来保证。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:58:- 原 generator 默认箭头占 2x2。现在 4/5 像素箭头最多占 3x3，需要新的边界检查。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:62:- 所有箭头都由合法模板构造：4 像素时仅一个臂端延长，5 像素时双臂延长。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:63:- 生成器仍采用 output-first：先给每个箭头选定总步数、段长和反射墙，再回填输入。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:64:- 箭头、墙、射线轨迹彼此不重叠；所有坐标都做 in-bounds 检查。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:70:- 解题者能直接看到：5 像素箭头比 4 像素箭头多一个同色附加格，而且它的输出轨迹稳定更长。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:76:- 没有远距离 marker；所有编码都贴在箭头本体上，局部可读性好。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:77:- 箭头、墙、轨迹之间不叠压；每个箭头颜色唯一，避免同色对象难以配对。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/29/code.py:93:- Solver 假设每个箭头连通块恰好匹配唯一合法模板。Generator 只放合法 4/5 像素模板。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ces