still extracted from the arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:34:      reason: the arrow shape itself does not encode whether to start horizontal\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:47:      arrow gives (dr, dc) = (1, 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:52:      same arrow gives latent (dr, dc) = (1, 1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:71:    a plain straight line. The generator therefore forces at least one arrow to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:77:    rule rather than adding a hidden per-arrow bit not encoded by the input.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:87:  - arrow blockers:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:89:      through the source arrow. So arrow cells can remain hard blockers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:99:    arrow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:101:    wall and must be in-bounds, unused, and not an arrow cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:109:    straight corridor implied by the arrow direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:110:  - In output, at least one arrow visibly uses both axes and turns multiple\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:117:  - Only three visual object types remain: L-arrows, isolated wall pixels, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:119:  - The generator rejects overlaps and self-intersections, so different arrows do\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:125:  - The ray always starts in the arrow color and only changes when it frontally\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/code.py:133:  - assumption: all arrows use the same horizontal-first convention.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/24/cod