，忽略箭头默认转向\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:17:#          red(2)  = 执行箭头给出的转向\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:19:#      若 c 处是红标记，则自上而下的信号会在箭头中心右转进入水平槽，原本在水平槽上的信号会向下落到该列；\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:20:#      若 c 处是蓝标记，则即使中心箭头看起来在提示右转，垂直信号仍保持向下，水平信号仍保持向右。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:21:#      因而“箭头提供默认 turn family，颜色决定是否真的执行这次 turn”，蓝色就是显式的优先级覆盖案例。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:24:#    - 箭头家族只保留两类（左右交换槽），交叉颜色也只保留两类（直行 / 转弯），总离散档位很少，便于从 2-4 个样例归纳。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:26:#      最终端点配对，否则这题就退化成“只读箭头”。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:27:#    - token 颜色池避开箭头颜色 4/5，只与 red/blue 有轻度复用；这种复用通过结构区分：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:31:#    - 原 _trace_wire 依赖“交叉处直行优先”即可正确；在本变体里，纯箭头交叉和红色交叉都可能要求立刻离开当前方向，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:32:#      因此必须先识别箭头中心，再看是否有红/蓝覆盖。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:33:#    - 原 track_mask = 非背景减 token，会把箭头对角装饰误当轨道支路。新版只把 8/9、红蓝交叉夹子和“解码出的箭头中心”\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:37:#    - 原 9-rect 识别只把 (5,8) 当作管道邻接。新版必须把 1/2/4/5 都视为 wire-like，否则矩形贴着箭头或交叉时会漏掉面连接。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:41:#    - 箭头对角装饰在同一方向家族内允许放在上侧或下侧；生成器按“上侧优先，否则下侧”的方式放置，避免相邻 crossover row\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:43:#    - color-9 矩形只允许覆盖 0/8，不允许吞掉箭头中心、红蓝夹子或对角装饰，否则人类无法恢复两层路由线索。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:47:#    - 观察者可以同时看到：交叉中心出现彩色箭头、两侧再出现红/蓝成对夹子。相同箭头家族在多个交叉重复出现，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:48:#      但红蓝会把这些交叉分成“执行箭头转向”和“无视箭头直行”两类。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:49:#    - 当同一条水平槽上同时有红和蓝时，输出里的 token 排列会显示：有些列真的交换了信号，有些列虽然也有箭头却没有交换。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:50:#      这正是“颜色优先覆盖默认箭头”的可视证据。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:53:#    - 主线仍保持 8/9 的大块结构；箭头只占交叉中心和一个对角像素，红蓝标记只占中心左右两格，没有额外铺满局部区域。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:54:#    - token、箭头、交叉夹子、9-rect 各自的几何角色固定，视觉上容易分层：3x3 token、正交主线、矩形块、交叉提示。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:57:#    - 颜色变化只承担两类局部语义：4/5 是箭头方向家族，1/2 是“是否执行该箭头”的控制位。不存在隐藏的颜色算术或排序。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:58:#    - 蓝色交叉是关键：它与红色交叉共享同类箭头，但输出行为不同，因此解题者能从少量样例学到优先级而不是把箭头当唯一规则。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:61:#    - solver 假设每个箭头中心都带有同家族的单个对角装饰，generator 的 _place_arrow_marker() 保证这一点。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:62:#    - solver 假设每个带红蓝夹子的交叉一定也是一个已解码箭头中心；generator 在每个被彩色控制的交叉上总是先放箭头再放夹子。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:66:#    - 生成器额外计算“arrow-only 路由”和“融合规则路由”的底部落点差异；若二者完全一致，则说明蓝色覆盖没有实际生效，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:176:def _find_arrow_markers(g: np.ndarray) -> dict[tuple[int, int], int]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:177:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return {center: hdir} for decoded arrow-family junction markers.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:203:    arrow_markers: dict[tuple[int, int], int],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:205:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return {arrow_center: PASS_MARK|TURN_MARK} for controlled interior crossings.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:209:    for r, c in arrow_markers:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:243:def _turn_dir_at_arrow(d: tuple[int, int], hdir: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:268:    arrow_markers: dict[tuple[int, int], int],\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:272:    Follow one wire component using arrow-family defaults, red/blue overrides, and 9-rect pass-through.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:274:    Pure arrow junctions always apply their turn family. At interior crossings, blue keeps the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:275:    current direction while red executes that same arrow-family turn.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:282:            raise AssertionError(\\\"wire trace looped under arrow+color routing\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:309:        arrow_hdir = arrow_markers.get(cur)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:310:        if arrow_hdir is not None:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:314:                nd = _turn_dir_at_arrow(d, arrow_hdir)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:351:    Route colored 3x3 tokens through pipe networks whose default turns come from arrow junctions, but whose crossings can overrule those arrows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:356:    - Some junction centers are colored arrow markers (4/5) with a matching diagonal decoration; some of those same junctions also carry blue/red side markers that control the crossing behavior.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:361:    - At an arrow-only junction, the signal follows the arrow's turn family. At an arrow+color crossing, red executes that turn while blue forces straight-through motion instead.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:365:    - The new challenge is two-layer routing: arrows define the default local turn map, but blue crossings visibly override that default. Correct endpoint pairing therefore depends on learning both the arrow family and the color priority.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:373:    arrow_markers = _find_arrow_markers(g)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:379:    for p in arrow_markers:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:392:    crossing_controls = _find_crossing_controls(track_mask, g, arrow_markers)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:426:                    end, dd = _trace_wire(comp, ep, (-odr, -odc), h, w, rects_9, arrow_markers, crossing_controls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:435:                    end, dd = _trace_wire(comp, ep, (-odr, -odc), h, w, rects_9, arrow_markers, crossing_controls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:506:def _place_arrow_marker(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, hdir: int) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:570:    Draw continuous channel columns plus arrow-marked row transfers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:572:    Each interior crossing gets both an arrow-family center and a red/blue control pair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:573:    Blue keeps straight; red executes the arrow family's swap turn.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:595:        if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, src_col, hdir):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:596:            raise AssertionError(\\\"failed to place source arrow marker\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:597:        if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, dst_col, hdir):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:598:            raise AssertionError(\\\"failed to place destination arrow marker\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:610:            if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, c, hdir):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:611:                raise AssertionError(\\\"failed to place interior arrow marker\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:642:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Attempt to place one color-9 rectangle without swallowing arrow/color controls.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:818:    arrow_only_bottom = _bottom_slots(_simulate_rows(n, row_specs, force_all_turn=True))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:819:    priority_effect = sum(int(a != b) for a, b in zip(actual_bottom, arrow_only_bottom))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:861:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Helper for diagnostics of the fused arrow+crossing-control behavior.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头直线贯穿射线\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:23:#    - D3/0: the external source object becomes an arrow sprite with one ring tip\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:27:#    Example: an arrow touching the top ring at column c points downward into the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:29:#    entire interior column from top to bottom. If the arrow is two-colored, the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:31:#    it. A bottom-touching arrow at the same column would paint the same geometry\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:37:#    - there are 2-3 arrows per grid, not just one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:38:#    - arrows can start from either of two opposite sides of the chosen axis\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:39:#    - monochrome and two-color arrows both appear\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:40:#    - at least one arrow per sample is two-color so direction is behaviorally\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:43:#    either vertical rays (top/bottom arrows) or horizontal rays (left/right\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:44:#    arrows). That avoids row/column crossings that would otherwise create noisy\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:49:#    - useful components no longer have >=2 ring touches; each arrow has exactly 1\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:52:#    - U-pairs are incompatible with \\\"one arrow -> one through-line\\\", so they are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:55:#    has the local arrow-head geometry for that side, then derives the full line\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:60:#    then converts each line into a single external arrow with:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:71:#    plainly an inward-pointing arrow attached to one side of the frame. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:82:#    Colors are structural, not id-based. Monochrome arrows produce solid rays.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:83:#    Two-color arrows alternate along the shaft and continue that alternation in\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:90:#    component has one touch plus an arrow head, and the output is full-span\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:96:#    - that ring cell belongs to a valid arrow-head pattern for one side\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:98:#    - useful arrows do not intersect in the cropped output\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:100:#    per sample, dedicated palette colors, and explicit arrow-shape validation in\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:208:def _has_arrow_tip(coords: set[tuple[int, int]], tip: tuple[int, int], side: str) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:298:def _place_arrow_component(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:327:    Reconstruct full-span interior rays from external arrows around a framed rectangle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:331:    - Useful external components are inward-pointing arrows. Each arrow has exactly one tip cell\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:336:    - Map each arrow tip to the corresponding interior boundary cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:339:    - Monochrome arrows paint solid rays; two-color arrows alternate starting from the tip color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:342:    - The arrow no longer encodes two endpoints. Its single ring tip fixes the line position, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:343:      the side/orientation of the arrow determines which full-span straight ray must be drawn.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:382:        if side is None or not _has_arrow_tip(coords, tip, side):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:457:    Every sample contains at least one monochrome arrow and one two-color arrow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:467:def _arrow_specs(side: str, idx: int, H: int, W: int, r0: int, c0: int, r1: int, c1: int):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:586:        inner, backbone, head = _arrow_specs(side, idx, H, W, r0, c0, r1, c1)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:600:        if not _place_arrow_component(grid, comp_mask, backbone, head, colors, bg):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/25/code.py:29:# - The variant is intentionally narrow rather than fully free-form:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:11:   - Objects stay the same as the base task: 3-pixel L-shaped arrows plus mono-color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:61:   - No overlaps are allowed among arrows, walls, or traversed cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:95:def _is_arrow_pts(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:103:def _arrow_dir_and_start(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:129:    Trace diagonal rays from L-shaped arrows with fused timing + rendering rules.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:143:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:144:    arrows: list[tuple[int, list[tuple[int, int]]]] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:148:            if _is_arrow_pts(pts):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:149:                arrows.append((int(col), pts))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:150:                arrow_cells |= set(pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:155:        if (int(r), int(c)) not in arrow_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:160:    for start_col, pts in arrows:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:161:        info = _arrow_dir_and_start(pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:182:            if (nr, nc) in arrow_cells:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:235:def _arrow_points(sr: int, sc: int, dr: int, dc: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:313:    n_arrows = _rng.randint(2, 4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:316:    arrow_colors = palette[:n_arrows]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:328:    for ai in range(n_arrows):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:329:        color = int(arrow_colors[ai])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:347:            arrow_pts = _arrow_points(sr, sc, dr, dc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:348:            arrow_set = set(arrow_pts)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:349:            if any(not (0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W) or (r, c) in occupied for r, c in arrow_pts):\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:377:                    if pos in occupied or pos in ray_set or pos in arrow_set or pos in planned_walls:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:412:                forbidden = occupied | ray_set | arrow_set | set(planned_walls) | set(input_walls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:448:                if pos in occupied or pos in ray_set or pos in arrow_set or pos in planned_walls:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:466:            new_cells = set(arrow_pts) | ray_set | set(planned_walls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:467:            expected = len(arrow_pts) + len(ray_set) + len(planned_walls)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:471:            for r, c in arrow_pts:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:23:      - 原题的几何对象不变：单色 3 像素 L 形箭头、单色墙、45 度对角线射线、侧碰反射。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:26:      - 每个箭头背后增加一条固定水平 1x3 提示条，left->right 给出该箭头的颜色循环列表。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:29:        A = 箭头自身颜色，B = 当前反射阶段的活动颜色。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:36:      - 箭头仍是 2x2 bbox 缺一角的 L 形，缺角决定发射方向，直角顶点是起点。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:37:      - 提示条固定放在箭头“后侧”，始终是水平 3 格，所以视觉上像局部图例而不是墙。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:40:      - 设箭头色 A=2，提示条是 [4, 8, 3]。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:50:      - 轨迹周期固定为 AABB，而不是任意模式；这样人类可以把规律归纳为“箭头色两格、当前循环色两格”。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:58:      - `wall_cells = non-bg minus arrow_cells` 原本默认除箭头外都是墙；加入提示条后必须把 hint cells 排除。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:63:      - 提示条是多色 1x3，不能被误识别成箭头，也不能被当作墙参与反射。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:68:      - 先放箭头和提示条，再规划对角线路径和墙。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:75:      - 提示条紧贴箭头，颜色来源是局部且可配对的。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:81:      - 提示条固定在箭头后侧，不进入主要轨迹区域。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code      if r in (r0, r1) or c in (c0, c1)\\\\n    }\\\\n    missing = list(border - pts)\\\\n    if len(missing) != 1 or pts - border:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    # The frame interior must be blank in the input.\\\\n    if np.any(g[r0 + 1 : r1, c0 + 1 : c1] != BG):\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    gr, gc = missing[0]\\\\n    if gr == r0 and c0 < gc < c1:\\\\n        direction = \\\\\\\"up\\\\\\\"\\\\n    elif gr == r1 and c0 < gc < c1:\\\\n        direction = \\\\\\\"down\\\\\\\"\\\\n    elif gc == c0 and r0 < gr < r1:\\\\n        direction = \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\"\\\\n    elif gc == c1 and r0 < gr < r1:\\\\n        direction = \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\"\\\\n    else:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    return {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\": (int(r0), int(c0), int(r1), int(c1)),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\": int(comp[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"gap\\\\\\\": (int(gr), int(gc)),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"direction\\\\\\\": direction,\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _classify_edge_block(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int], h: int, w: int) -> str | None:\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox\\\\n    distances = {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\": r0,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\": h - 1 - r1,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\": c0,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\": w - 1 - c1,\\\\n    }\\\\n    side, dist = min(distances.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\\\\n    if dist > 3:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    center_r2 = r0 + r1\\\\n    center_c2 = c0 + c1\\\\n    if side in (\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\"):\\\\n        if center_c2 <= 4 or center_c2 >= 2 * w - 6:\\\\n            return None\\\\n    else:\\\\n        if center_r2 <= 4 or center_r2 >= 2 * h - 6:\\\\n            return None\\\\n    return side\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _find_edge_blocks(g: np.ndarray, frame_components: set[int]) -> dict[str, list[dict]]:\\\\n    h, w = g.shape\\\\n    blocks = {side: [] for side in (\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\")}\\\\n    for idx, comp in enumerate(_same_color_components(g)):\\\\n        if idx in frame_components:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        r0, c0, r1, c1 = comp[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        bh = r1 - r0 + 1\\\\n        bw = c1 - c0 + 1\\\\n        if bh < 2 or bw < 2 or bh > 4 or bw > 4:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        if comp[\\\\\\\"area\\\\\\\"] != bh * bw:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        side = _classify_edge_block(comp[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"], h, w)\\\\n        if side is None:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        blocks[side].append(\\\\n            {\\\\n                \\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\": int(comp[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]),\\\\n                \\\\\\\"area\\\\\\\": int(comp[\\\\\\\"area\\\\\\\"]),\\\\n                \\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\": comp[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"],\\\\n            }\\\\n        )\\\\n\\\\n    for side in blocks:\\\\n        blocks[side].sort(key=lambda b: (-int(b[\\\\\\\"area\\\\\\\"]), int(b[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][0]), int(b[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][1])))\\\\n    return blocks\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _find_frames_and_component_ids(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[dict], set[int]]:\\\\n    frames: list[dict] = []\\\\n    frame_component_ids: set[int] = set()\\\\n    comps = _same_color_components(g)\\\\n    for idx, comp in enumerate(comps):\\\\n        frame = _frame_from_component(g, comp)\\\\n        if frame is not None:\\\\n            frames.append(frame)\\\\n            frame_component_ids.add(idx)\\\\n    return frames, frame_component_ids\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Fill each hollow frame with the edge-palette color indicated by its missing side.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - The background is black (0).\\\\n    - Several one-pixel-thick rectangular hollow frames are scattered in the interior; each frame has one same-color border with exactly one non-corner border pixel missing.\\\\n    - Small isolated solid color blocks sit near the top, bottom, left, and right grid edges and do not overlap any frame.\\\\n    - Multiple blocks on the same edge direction are visibly ordered by their block area.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - Detect which side of each frame contains the single missing border pixel: top, bottom, left, or right.\\\\n    - Match that side to the corresponding edge color pool: top->up, bottom->down, left->left, right->right.\\\\n    - For each direction, sort its frames from left to right and then top to bottom, and sort that edge's color blocks by area from large to small.\\\\n    - Fill every blank interior pixel of each frame with the assigned edge-block color, leaving the border and the missing border gap unchanged.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The tiny gap in a frame is a hidden direction key, and that direction selects a visible color pool on the matching grid edge.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n    frames, frame_component_ids = _find_frames_and_component_ids(g)\\\\n    pools = _find_edge_blocks(g, frame_component_ids)\\\\n\\\\n    for direction in DIRS:\\\\n        side = DIR_TO_SIDE[direction]\\\\n        group = [f for f in frames if f[\\\\\\\"direction\\\\\\\"] == direction]\\\\n        group.sort(key=lambda f: (int(f[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][1]), int(f[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][0])))\\\\n        assert len(pools[side]) >= len(group), \\\\\\\"each frame direction needs a matching edge color block\\\\\\\"\\\\n        for frame, block in zip(group, pools[side], strict=False):\\\\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = frame[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n            interior = out[r0 + 1 : r1, c0 + 1 : c1]\\\\n            interior[interior == BG] = int(block[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"])\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n# ------------------------------ generator ------------------------------\\\\n\\\\nGRID_SIZE_RANGE = (24, 30)\\\\nFRAME_H_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nFRAME_W_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nGEN_RETRIES = 500\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _can_place(mask: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, h: int, w: int, pad: int = 1) -> bool:\\\\n    H, W = mask.shape\\\\n    if r < 0 or c < 0 or r + h > H or c + w > W:\\\\n        return False\\\\n    rr0 = max(0, r - pad)\\\\n    cc0 = max(0, c - pad)\\\\n    rr1 = min(H, r + h + pad)\\\\n    cc1 = min(W, c + w + pad)\\\\n    return not bool(mask[rr0:rr1, cc0:cc1].any())\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:43:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_22\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/2.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:44:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_22\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/2.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nBG = 0\\\\nCOLOR_COUNT = 10\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 500\\\\nPLACEMENT_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\nSEGMENT_PADDING = 1\\\\nRECT_PADDING = 1\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _components_for_color(grid: np.ndarray, color: int) -> list[list[tuple[int, int]]]:\\\\n    mask = grid == int(color)\\\\n    seen = np.zeros(mask.shape, dtype=bool)\\\\n    comps: list[list[tuple[int, int]]] = []\\\\n    height, width = mask.shape\\\\n\\\\n    for r in range(height):\\\\n        for c in range(width):\\\\n            if not mask[r, c] or seen[r, c]:\\\\n                continue\\\\n\\\\n            stack = [(r, c)]\\\\n            seen[r, c] = True\\\\n            coords: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\\\\n            while stack:\\\\n                rr, cc = stack.pop()\\\\n                coords.append((rr, cc))\\\\n                for dr, dc in ((-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)):\\\\n                    nr, nc = rr + dr, cc + dc\\\\n                    if 0 <= nr < height and 0 <= nc < width and mask[nr, nc] and not seen[nr, nc]:\\\\n                        seen[nr, nc] = True\\\\n                        stack.append((nr, nc))\\\\n            comps.append(coords)\\\\n\\\\n    return comps\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _line_info(coords: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> dict:\\\\n    rows = [r for r, _c in coords]\\\\n    cols = [c for _r, c in coords]\\\\n    r0, r1 = min(rows), max(rows)\\\\n    c0, c1 = min(cols), max(cols)\\\\n\\\\n    if r0 == r1 and c0 < c1:\\\\n        expected = {(r0, c) for c in range(c0, c1 + 1)}\\\\n        assert set(coords) == expected, \\\\\\\"horizontal pieces must be solid line segments\\\\\\\"\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\": c1 - c0 + 1, \\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\": (r0, c0)}\\\\n\\\\n    if c0 == c1 and r0 < r1:\\\\n        expected = {(r, c0) for r in range(r0, r1 + 1)}\\\\n        assert set(coords) == expected, \\\\\\\"vertical pieces must be solid line segments\\\\\\\"\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\": r1 - r0 + 1, \\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\": (r0, c0)}\\\\n\\\\n    raise AssertionError(\\\\\\\"each foreground component must be one horizontal or vertical segment of length at least 2\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _draw_frame(out: np.ndarray, color: int, r0: int, c0: int, height: int, width: int) -> None:\\\\n    rows, cols = out.shape\\\\n    assert height >= 2 and width >= 2\\\\n    assert 0 <= r0 and 0 <= c0 and r0 + height <= rows and c0 + width <= cols\\\\n\\\\n    cells = set()\\\\n    for c in range(c0, c0 + width):\\\\n        cells.add((r0, c))\\\\n        cells.add((r0 + height - 1, c))\\\\n    for r in range(r0, r0 + height):\\\\n        cells.add((r, c0))\\\\n        cells.add((r, c0 + width - 1))\\\\n\\\\n    for r, c in cells:\\\\n        assert int(out[r, c]) in (BG, int(color)), \\\\\\\"assembled rectangles must not overlap\\\\\\\"\\\\n        out[r, c] = int(color)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _present_colors(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[int]:\\\\n    colors: list[int] = []\\\\n    seen = {BG}\\\\n    for value in grid.ravel():\\\\n        color = int(value)\\\\n        if color not in seen:\\\\n            seen.add(color)\\\\n            colors.append(color)\\\\n    return colors\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Reassemble scattered same-color line segments into complete rectangular frames.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - The background is black.\\\\n    - Each non-background color appears as exactly four disconnected one-pixel-thick line segments.\\\\n    - For each color, two segments are horizontal with the same length and two are vertical with the same length.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - Group the segments by color and identify the two horizontal and two vertical pieces in each group.\\\\n    - The horizontal length gives the rectangle width, and the vertical length gives the rectangle height.\\\\n    - Draw that color's hollow rectangular border with its upper-left corner at the start endpoint of the most upper-left segment in the group.\\\\n    - Clear the scattered fragments; the rectangle interiors and all other cells remain background.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\n    Same-colored fragments are not independent objects: they are the four translated sides of one hidden rectangle.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    assert g.ndim == 2\\\\n\\\\n    out = np.full_like(g, BG)\\\\n    for color in _present_colors(g):\\\\n        segments = [_line_info(comp) for comp in _components_for_color(g, color)]\\\\n        assert len(segments) == 4, \\\\\\\"each color must have exactly four line segments\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n        horizontals = [seg for seg in segments if seg[\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        verticals = [seg for seg in segments if seg[\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        assert len(horizontals) == 2 and len(verticals) == 2\\\\n        assert len({int(seg[\\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\"]) for seg in horizontals}) == 1\\\\n        assert len({int(seg[\\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\"]) for seg in verticals}) == 1\\\\n\\\\n        width = int(horizontals[0][\\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\"])\\\\n        height = int(verticals[0][\\\\\\\"length\\\\\\\"])\\\\n        anchor_r, anchor_c = min((tuple(seg[\\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\"]) for seg in segments), key=lambda pt: (pt[0], pt[1]))\\\\n        _draw_frame(out, color, int(anchor_r), int(anchor_c), height, width)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _segment_cells(kind: str, r0: int, c0: int, length: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\\\n    if kind == \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\":\\\\n        return [(int(r0), int(c)) for c in range(int(c0), int(c0) + int(length))]\\\\n    return [(int(r), int(c0)) for r in range(int(r0), int(r0) + int(length))]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _cells_fit(cells: list[tuple[int, int]], rows: int, cols: int) -> bool:\\\\n    return all(0 <= r < rows and 0 <= c < cols for r, c in cells)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _can_place_segment(occupied: np.ndarray, cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\\\\n    rows, cols = occupied.shape\\\\n    if not _cells_fit(cells, rows, cols):\\\\n        return False\\\\n    for r, c in cells:\\\\n        r0 = max(0, r - SEGMENT_PADDING)\\\\n        r1 = min(rows, r + SEGMENT_PADDING + 1)\\\\n        c0 = max(0, c - SEGMENT_PADDING)\\\\n        c1 = min(cols, c + SEGMENT_PADDING + 1)\\\\n        if bool(occupied[r0:r1, c0:c1].any()):\\\\n            return False\\\\n    return True\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _paint_cells(grid: np.ndarray, occupied: np.ndarray, cells: list[tuple[int, int]], color: int) -> None:\\\\n    for r, c in cells:\\\\n        grid[r, c] = int(color)\\\\n        occupied[r, c] = True\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _place_segment(\\\\n    grid: np.ndarray,\\\\n    occupied: np.ndarray,\\\\n    rng: np.random.Generator,\\\\n    color: int,\\\\n    kind: str,\\\\n    length: int,\\\\n    min_r: int = 0,\\\\n    min_c: int = 0,\\\\n) -> bool:\\\\n    rows, cols = grid.shape\\\\n    max_r = rows - 1 if kind == \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\" else rows - int(length)\\\\n    max_c = cols - int(length) if kind == \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\" else cols - 1\\\\n    if min_r > max_r or min_c > max_c:\\\\n        return False\\\\n\\\\n    for _ in range(PLACEMENT_ATTEMPTS):\\\\n        r0 = int(rng.integers(min_r, max_r + 1))\\\\n        c0 = int(rng.integers(min_c, max_c + 1))\\\\n        cells = _segment_cells(kind, r0, c0, length)\\\\n        if _can_place_segment(occupied, cells):\\\\n            _paint_cells(grid, occupied, cells, color)\\\\n            return True\\\\n\\\\n    candidates = [(r, c) for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1) for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1)]\\\\n    rng.shuffle(candidates)\\\\n    for r0, c0 in candidates:\\\\n        cells = _segment_cells(kind, r0, c0, length)\\\\n        if _can_place_segment(occupied, cells):\\\\n            _paint_cells(grid, occupied, cells, color)\\\\n            return True\\\\n    return False\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _bboxes_overlap(a: tuple[int, int, int, int], b: tuple[int, int, int, int], padding: int) -> bool:\\\\n    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = a\\\\n    br0, bc0, br1, bc1 = b\\\\n    return not (\\\\n        ar1 + padding < br0\\\\n        or br1 + padding < ar0\\\\n        or ac1 + padding < bc0\\\\n        or bc1 + padding < ac0\\\\n    )\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _place_rectangles(\\\\n    rng: np.random.Generator, rows: int, cols: int, colors: list[int]\\\\n) -> list[dict] | None:\\\\n    rects: list[dict] = []\\\\n\\\\n    for color in colors:\\\\n        placed = False\\\\n        for _ in range(PLACEMENT_ATTEMPTS):\\\\n            height = int(rng.integers(3, 8))\\\\n            width = int(rng.integers(3, 8))\\\\n            max_r = rows - height - 2\\\\n            max_c = cols - width - 2\\\\n            if max_r < 0 or max_c < 0:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            r0 = int(rng.integers(0, max_r + 1))\\\\n            c0 = int(rng.integers(0, max_c + 1))\\\\n            bbox = (r0, c0, r0 + height - 1, c0 + width - 1)\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:45:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/3.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:46:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/3.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nfrom collections import deque\\\\nimport random\\\\n\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nBLUE = 1\\\\nGREY = 5\\\\nSEED_COLORS = (2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9)\\\\nNEIGHBORS4 = ((-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _spans(length: int, separators: list[int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\\\n    spans: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\\\\n    start = 0\\\\n    for sep in separators:\\\\n        assert start < sep, \\\\\\\"separator lines must leave nonempty regions\\\\\\\"\\\\n        spans.append((start, sep - 1))\\\\n        start = sep + 1\\\\n    assert start < length, \\\\\\\"separator lines must leave a final nonempty region\\\\\\\"\\\\n    spans.append((start, length - 1))\\\\n    return spans\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _separator_spans(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], list[tuple[int, int]]]:\\\\n    h, w = g.shape\\\\n    sep_rows = [r for r in range(h) if np.all(g[r, :] == GREY)]\\\\n    sep_cols = [c for c in range(w) if np.all(g[:, c] == GREY)]\\\\n    assert sep_rows and sep_cols, \\\\\\\"expected full grey horizontal and vertical separator lines\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    row_spans = _spans(h, sep_rows)\\\\n    col_spans = _spans(w, sep_cols)\\\\n    assert len({r1 - r0 + 1 for r0, r1 in row_spans}) == 1, \\\\\\\"row regions must have equal height\\\\\\\"\\\\n    assert len({c1 - c0 + 1 for c0, c1 in col_spans}) == 1, \\\\\\\"column regions must have equal width\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return row_spans, col_spans\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _is_connected(mask: np.ndarray) -> bool:\\\\n    pts = np.argwhere(mask)\\\\n    if pts.size == 0:\\\\n        return False\\\\n    h, w = mask.shape\\\\n    start = tuple(map(int, pts[0]))\\\\n    seen = {start}\\\\n    q: deque[tuple[int, int]] = deque([start])\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        r, c = q.popleft()\\\\n        for dr, dc in NEIGHBORS4:\\\\n            rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\\\\n            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and mask[rr, cc] and (rr, cc) not in seen:\\\\n                seen.add((rr, cc))\\\\n                q.append((rr, cc))\\\\n    return len(seen) == int(np.count_nonzero(mask))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _depth_map(mask: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return each template pixel's inward erosion layer; non-template cells are -1.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    h, w = mask.shape\\\\n    depth = np.full((h, w), -1, dtype=int)\\\\n    q: deque[tuple[int, int]] = deque()\\\\n\\\\n    for r, c in np.argwhere(mask):\\\\n        r = int(r)\\\\n        c = int(c)\\\\n        boundary = False\\\\n        for dr, dc in NEIGHBORS4:\\\\n            rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\\\\n            if not (0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w) or not mask[rr, cc]:\\\\n                boundary = True\\\\n                break\\\\n        if boundary:\\\\n            depth[r, c] = 0\\\\n            q.append((r, c))\\\\n\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        r, c = q.popleft()\\\\n        for dr, dc in NEIGHBORS4:\\\\n            rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\\\\n            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and mask[rr, cc] and depth[rr, cc] < 0:\\\\n                depth[rr, cc] = depth[r, c] + 1\\\\n                q.append((rr, cc))\\\\n\\\\n    assert np.all(depth[mask] >= 0), \\\\\\\"every template pixel must receive a layer\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return depth\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Grow seed-colored concentric rings inward inside each blue template tile.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - The background is black and full grey separator rows and columns split the grid into equal rectangular regions.\\\\n    - A region is either empty black or contains one connected blue template shape with zero or more same-colored seed pixels on template cells.\\\\n    - Seed colors are any colors other than black, grey, and blue; their positions inside the template do not encode direction or placement.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each region with a template and seeds, count the seed pixels N and read their shared color.\\\\n    - Treat the template boundary as layer 0, where boundary means template pixels 4-adjacent to black space, a grey separator, or the region edge.\\\\n    - Moving inward by repeated 4-neighbor erosion gives layers 1, 2, and so on; recolor only layers 1 through N with the seed color.\\\\n    - Layer 0 and any layers deeper than N are blue, so the original seed pixels are overwritten by their final layer color.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\n    - The number of seed pixels controls the inward coloring depth; seed locations are irrelevant once their count and color are known.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    assert g.ndim == 2 and g.size > 0, \\\\\\\"expected a nonempty 2D grid\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    row_spans, col_spans = _separator_spans(g)\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n\\\\n    for r0, r1 in row_spans:\\\\n        for c0, c1 in col_spans:\\\\n            tile = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\\\\n            seed_mask = (tile != BLACK) & (tile != GREY) & (tile != BLUE)\\\\n            template = (tile == BLUE) | seed_mask\\\\n            if not np.any(template):\\\\n                assert np.all(tile == BLACK), \\\\\\\"empty regions must be black\\\\\\\"\\\\n                continue\\\\n            assert np.any(tile == BLUE), \\\\\\\"nonempty regions must include a blue template\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n            region = out[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\\\\n            if not np.any(seed_mask):\\\\n                region[template] = BLUE\\\\n                continue\\\\n\\\\n            seed_values = np.unique(tile[seed_mask])\\\\n            assert seed_values.size == 1, \\\\\\\"all seeds in one region must share one color\\\\\\\"\\\\n            seed_color = int(seed_values[0])\\\\n            seed_count = int(np.count_nonzero(seed_mask))\\\\n\\\\n            depth = _depth_map(template)\\\\n            region[template] = BLUE\\\\n            fill = template & (depth >= 1) & (depth <= seed_count)\\\\n            region[fill] = seed_color\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator ---------------\\\\n\\\\nTILE_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTILE_COLS_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTILE_SIDE_RANGE = (5, 8)\\\\nACTIVE_REGION_MIN = 2\\\\nACTIVE_REGION_MAX = 8\\\\nMAX_SEEDS = 5\\\\nGEN_RETRIES = 400\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _valid_tile_sizes(count: int) -> list[int]:\\\\n    return [size for size in range(TILE_SIDE_RANGE[0], TILE_SIDE_RANGE[1] + 1) if count * size + count - 1 <= 30]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _base_grid(tile_rows: int, tile_cols: int, tile_h: int, tile_w: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    h = tile_rows * tile_h + tile_rows - 1\\\\n    w = tile_cols * tile_w + tile_cols - 1\\\\n    grid = np.full((h, w), BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\n    for r in range(tile_h, h, tile_h + 1):\\\\n        grid[r, :] = GREY\\\\n    for c in range(tile_w, w, tile_w + 1):\\\\n        grid[:, c] = GREY\\\\n    return grid\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _tile_origin(tile_r: int, tile_c: int, tile_h: int, tile_w: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\\\n    return tile_r * (tile_h + 1), tile_c * (tile_w + 1)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _boundary_cells(mask: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\\\n    h, w = mask.shape\\\\n    cells: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\\\\n    for r, c in np.argwhere(mask):\\\\n        r = int(r)\\\\n        c = int(c)\\\\n        if any(\\\\n            not (0 <= r + dr < h and 0 <= c + dc < w) or not mask[r + dr, c + dc]\\\\n            for dr, dc in NEIGHBORS4\\\\n        ):\\\\n            cells.append((r, c))\\\\n    return cells\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _random_notched_box(height: int, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    mask = np.ones((height, width), dtype=bool)\\\\n    removals = random.randint(1, max(1, (height + width) // 2))\\\\n    for _ in range(removals):\\\\n        candidates = _boundary_cells(mask)\\\\n        random.shuffle(candidates)\\\\n        for r, c in candidates:\\\\n            trial = mask.copy()\\\\n            trial[r, c] = False\\\\n            if int(np.count_nonzero(trial)) < 6:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            if not _is_connected(trial):\\\\n                continue\\\\n            if int(_depth_map(trial).max()) < 1:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            mask = trial\\\\n            break\\\\n    return mask\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _diamond(radius: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    size = 2 * radius + 1\\\\n    mask = np.zeros((size, size), dtype=bool)\\\\n    for r in range(size):\\\\n        for c in range(size):\\\\n            if abs(r - radius) + abs(c - radius) <= radius:\\\\n                mask[r, c] = True\\\\n    return mask\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _thick_cross(height: int, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    mask = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=bool)\\\\n    cr = height // 2\\\\n    cc = width // 2\\\\n    mask[max(0, cr - 1) : min(height, cr + 2), :] = True\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:47:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_24\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"现在开始写 `/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/5.py`。解析逻辑会通过红/绿外壁组件找矩形房间，生成器会用预留掩码同时预留输入房间和输出盖印位置，避免对象粘连或输出覆盖。\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:48:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_25\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_change\\\",\\\"changes\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/5.py\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"add\\\"}],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_122058_gpt55_xhigh_missing/7__codegen_prompts__5.log:49:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_25\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_change\\\",\\\"changes\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/7/5.py\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"add\\\"}],\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\